ting – hydro infrastructure and tra"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal"}, {"alpha2": "BT", "alpha3": "BTN", "name_zh": "不丹", "name_en": "Bhutan"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://dialogue.earth/en/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:20.180954+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-10-02T17:27:22", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BT", "alpha3": "BTN", "name_zh": "不丹", "name_en": "Bhutan", "start": 31, "end": 37, "matched_text": "Bhutan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India", "start": 61, "end": 66, "matched_text": "India", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal", "start": 0, "end": 5, "matched_text": "Nepal", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "BT", "alpha3": "BTN", "name_zh": "不丹", "name_en": "Bhutan", "start": 46, "end": 52, "matched_text": "Bhutan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India", "start": 159, "end": 164, "matched_text": "India", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_d04c9e2c05ae12b77b1c", "record_id": "article_d04c9e2c05ae12b7", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02102026/chesapeake-bay-restoration-new-challenges", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02102026/chesapeake-bay-restoration-new-challenges", "title_original": "Chesapeake Bay Restoration Obstructed by Federal Policy Shift, Tribal Withdrawal", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-02T08:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "Two major challenges could complicate efforts to restore the Chesapeake Bay. First, a new executive order from President Donald Trump revoked the longstanding framework for coordinating federal efforts to protect the bay. Second, seven Virginia tribes withdrew from formal participation after the Chesapeake Bay Program partnership denied them the signatory status they sought. The new […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 389, "text_sha256": "039af9f2cff2cfbdd6ff629dce51f2fb564f3d9d275d27544376aabc48f2dd81", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:42.638914+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:42.652722+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-10-02T08:55:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_3152b34afeda1c9a29e9", "record_id": "article_3152b34afeda1c9a", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/10/from-community-based-to-community-led-conservation-in-kenya-interview-with-dickson-kaelo", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/10/from-community-based-to-community-led-conservation-in-kenya-interview-with-dickson-kaelo", "title_original": "From ‘community-based’ to ‘community-led conservation’ in Kenya: Interview with Dickson Kaelo", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-01T13:26:51+00:00", "source_text": "NEW YORK — Long before Dickson Kaelo became one of the leading voices for community conservancies in Kenya, conservation was something much more personal. He grew up with livestock. His father was a veterinarian. And he knew firsthand the uneasy relationship between pastoralist communities and wildlife: Lions killing cattle, elephants destroying crops, hyenas taking goats […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 378, "text_sha256": "7d6b0deb319690b52521f106d7d7c136932b12836a637a6a84cf0f69bdceda16", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.439092+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.456037+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-10-01T13:26:51", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya", "start": 58, "end": 63, "matched_text": "Kenya", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya", "start": 101, "end": 106, "matched_text": "Kenya", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f56ef7b7844a11a21484", "record_id": "article_f56ef7b7844a11a2", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/10/vantara-in-talks-with-brazil-on-strategic-cooperation-on-threatened-species-foia-documents-reveal", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/10/vantara-in-talks-with-brazil-on-strategic-cooperation-on-threatened-species-foia-documents-reveal", "title_original": "Vantara in talks with Brazil on ‘strategic cooperation’ on threatened species, FOIA documents reveal", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-01T11:01:06+00:00", "source_text": "Vantara, the billionaire-run Indian private zoo that houses more than 150,000 animals, discussed a “strategic conservation partnership” with authorities in Brazil, the world’s most biodiverse country, according to documents obtained by Mongabay under Brazil’s Freedom of Information Act (FOIA). Correspondence between Vantara representatives and Brazilian officials reveal that negotiations, initiated by Vantara, began in August […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 433, "text_sha256": "9bb140096114788d827eb42a8583244c467a78e3c6e1c347bb70f2528166de59", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.476601+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.496236+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-10-01T11:01:06", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 22, "end": 28, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 156, "end": 162, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c3c1c3845f64f9df4d6b", "record_id": "article_c3c1c3845f64f9df", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/09/philippine-eagle-habitat-study-maps-mining-risks-and-conservation-priorities", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/09/philippine-eagle-habitat-study-maps-mining-risks-and-conservation-priorities", "title_original": "Philippine eagle habitat study maps mining risks and conservation priorities", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-09-30T18:18:27+00:00", "source_text": "A new study mapping the likely nesting habitats of the iconic Philippine eagle in its main stronghold warns that the threat of habitat loss — a key driver of its disappearance across much of its range — still looms large for the critically endangered species. The study, published in Bird Conservation International, shows that approved […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 340, "text_sha256": "5f8298a5667360f78f1390297ef3b571febc103347210c3f01814ae57c267d93", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.667674+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [{"id": "adopted", "label_zh": "通过", "label_en": "Adopted", "start": 328, "end": 336, "evidence": "y endangered species. The study, published in Bird Conservation International, shows that approved […]"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:40.695203+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-09-30T18:18:27", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7edac928944f9f116c01", "record_id": "article_7edac928944f9f11", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/09/after-two-landfalls-in-mexico-hurricane-polos-rainmaking-journey-has-just-begun", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/09/after-two-landfalls-in-mexico-hurricane-polos-rainmaking-journey-has-just-begun", "title_original": "After two landfalls in Mexico, Hurricane Polo’s rainmaking journey has just begun", "title_zh": "在两次登陆墨西哥之后，飓风“波罗”制造降雨的征程才刚刚开始", "title_en": null, "summary_zh": "飓风“波罗”以二级强度登陆墨西哥下加利福尼亚半岛南部的拉斯巴兰卡斯附近，随后穿越并再次登陆墨西哥。尽管其风力已减弱，但来自该系统及前飓风“奥达利斯”的水汽正向美国西南部、中西部及南部平原输送，预计将引发多日的强降雨并可能导致局部洪水。", "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-09-29T17:37:53+00:00", "source_text": "Hurricane Polo stormed onto the coast of Mexico’s Baja California Sur on Monday night local time, making landfall just south of Las Barrancas at around 11 p.m. MST (2 a.m. EDT Tuesday ) as a high-end Category 2 storm with top sustained winds of 110 mph (175 km/h) and a central pressure of 965 mb. Polo was tied as the fourth-strongest hurricane on record to make landfall on the Baja Peninsula, and is one of only 10 Cat 2 or stronger hurricanes to hit the peninsula since record-keeping began in 1949 (Fig. 1). Satellite imagery showed Polo becoming more disheveled in the several hours prior to landfall, as intrusions of dry air, increasing wind shear, and the increasing influence of rugged terrain all took their toll.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 724, "text_sha256": "62b4954fc55c0cf92f91f560cdb9fb0db426e6539eb91b338936c732c88a0076", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:28.528258+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:28.564813+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-09-29T17:37:53", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 23, "end": 29, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 41, "end": 47, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 55, "end": 65, "matched_text": "California", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c5e63de3f8457c16be90", "record_id": "article_c5e63de3f8457c16", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/29092026/maui-wildfire-longterm-health-impacts-study", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/29092026/maui-wildfire-longterm-health-impacts-study", "title_original": "Long After Wildfire Smoke Is Gone, Heavy Metals Could Still Be Harming Survivors’ Lungs", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-09-29T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "After three years helping Maui wildfire survivors track their health progress, Dr. Martina L. Kamaka is used to seeing high levels of heavy metals in their bodies. A family medicine doctor, Kamaka is one of the physicians helping with the Maui Wildfire Exposure Study, a multi-year effort from the University of Hawai‘i to chronicle the […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 340, "text_sha256": "944f0054323dc5db202892902852ebf1c503c7fd3f7c273487639c65fb3dc96c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:43.152676+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 31, "end": 39, "evidence": "After three years helping Maui wildfire survivors track their health progress, Dr. Martina L. Kamaka is used to seeing high levels of heavy metals in their bodies. A family medici"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:43.212305+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-09-29T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_65ac9ec0ebc3653ea4d4", "record_id": "article_65ac9ec0ebc3653e", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/09/as-australias-kangaroo-numbers-rise-record-cull-renews-calls-for-other-control-methods", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/09/as-australias-kangaroo-numbers-rise-record-cull-renews-calls-for-other-control-methods", "title_original": "As Australia’s kangaroo numbers rise, record cull renews calls for other control methods", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-09-28T12:13:38+00:00", "source_text": "CANBERRA — Australia has a problem with the very creature that is its official national symbol: The kangaroo. Endemic to Australia, they live across the country, from north to south, and from east to west. Australia has four main kangaroo species: The red kangaroo (Osphranter rufus), the largest of all species, mainly found in the […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 336, "text_sha256": "8cc21d7fcffe79810b19f7d62d074a0b2ba11ea2460f5183c683665bb1a21ea0", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:41.076415+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:41.088376+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-09-28T12:13:38", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia", "start": 3, "end": 12, "matched_text": "Australia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia", "start": 11, "end": 20, "matched_text": "Australia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_1fb427f139038ec928fa", "record_id": "article_1fb427f139038ec9", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/28092026/thermal-justice-europe", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/28092026/thermal-justice-europe", "title_original": "Revealing the Invisible Injustice of Extreme Heat", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-09-28T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "The extreme heat scientists have warned about for decades came to Europe again this summer, killing at least 30,000 people like a silent, invisible plague. It came for poor people, the very young and very old, and those suffering from debilitating conditions. The final toll will likely be higher. A 2024 United Nations report estimated […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 340, "text_sha256": "1c7d9523998e695e93b274ca0ba6e67b5f66037ee63ad900a6a97ad9da4a70a8", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:43.904932+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:43.932003+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2