{"text_id": "text_a163de261f45be166754", "record_id": "article_a163de261f45be16", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/failed-environmental-safeguards-leave-coastal-bangladesh-facing-coal-pollution", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/failed-environmental-safeguards-leave-coastal-bangladesh-facing-coal-pollution", "title_original": "Failed environmental safeguards leave coastal Bangladesh facing coal pollution", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-28T15:15:19+00:00", "source_text": "Riaz Panchayet used to farm papaya, cucumber, okra and bananas on his land in Madhupur village, located in southern Bangladesh’s coastal Patuakhali district. These days, he runs a small tea stall near one of the gates of the Payra Power Plant, and worry has replaced the seasonal rhythm of harvests. “I notice a layer of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 324, "text_sha256": "79e91bb7674d7938a9fa322bd460b932f46af819772a356e25a0a3c05117da6c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:03.991103+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:04.100606+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-08-28T15:15:19", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh", "start": 46, "end": 56, "matched_text": "Bangladesh", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh", "start": 116, "end": 126, "matched_text": "Bangladesh", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_b7a7279dd11b46486438", "record_id": "article_b7a7279dd11b4648", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27082026/empoderando-a-las-comunidades-guatemaltecas-afectadas-por-el-plastico", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27082026/empoderando-a-las-comunidades-guatemaltecas-afectadas-por-el-plastico", "title_original": "Empoderando a las comunidades guatemaltecas afectadas por el plástico", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-27T22:40:41+00:00", "source_text": "Read this article in English. Esta historia cuenta con el apoyo del Centro Pulitzer. JALAPA, Guatemala—En una tarde calurosa y bochornosa, en el pequeño pueblo montañoso de El Duraznal, Soila Elizabeth Cruz recogía basura plástica atrapada en la tierra debajo de una cerca con alambre de púas, mientras los camiones pasaban zumbando. La comunidad se […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 353, "text_sha256": "a29901699b522e84e8b40cfffc1be92074bdb7bb1d64b889caa4a5acd2fbfa40", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:13.975628+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "GT", "alpha3": "GTM", "name_zh": "危地马拉", "name_en": "Guatemala"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "GT", "alpha3": "GTM", "name_zh": "危地马拉", "name_en": "Guatemala"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:13.987993+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-08-27T22:40:41", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "GT", "alpha3": "GTM", "name_zh": "危地马拉", "name_en": "Guatemala", "start": 93, "end": 102, "matched_text": "Guatemala", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_00776d45c7b6229bc8d4", "record_id": "article_00776d45c7b6229b", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/13-peccaries-sail-home-to-heal-a-costa-rican-forest", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/13-peccaries-sail-home-to-heal-a-costa-rican-forest", "title_original": "13 peccaries sail home to heal a Costa Rican forest", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-27T18:30:08+00:00", "source_text": "It’s after midnight, and veterinarian Dennise Ortiz Angulo is in the middle of Golfo Dulce, surrounded by shooting stars, bioluminescent water, and 13 boar-like beasts. “That moment, it felt like the movie Life of Pi,” Ortiz told Mongabay. After years of preparation, hours of fast-paced decision-making, and a tedious truck drive, Ortiz, 13 white-lipped peccaries […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 368, "text_sha256": "b9751da2a998cc368d58d60cc1fb0ce1ec547376e5142fc58cba8cd0a048eaf2", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:04.709813+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:04.730144+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-08-27T18:30:08", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_872c1744e71209722772", "record_id": "article_872c1744e7120972", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/08/tropical-storm-dolly-forms-in-the-atlantic", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/08/tropical-storm-dolly-forms-in-the-atlantic", "title_original": "Tropical Storm Dolly forms in the Atlantic", "title_zh": "热带风暴“多莉”在大西洋形成", "title_en": null, "summary_zh": "热带风暴“多莉”于周四上午在大西洋热带地区形成，最大持续风速达到每小时 40 英里。该系统预计在抵达加勒比海东北部群岛之前减弱，带来降雨的同时风力影响有限，有望缓和当地的极端干旱状况。", "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-27T18:03:32+00:00", "source_text": "[ Haz clic aquí para leer esta nota en español] Tropical Storm Dolly formed in the tropical Atlantic on Thursday morning. After reviewing satellite imagery of Invest 96L, the National Hurricane Center determined that the system had developed a well-defined center of circulation on Thursday morning and had acquired tropical characteristics, with maximum sustained winds of at least 40 mph (65 km/h). Dolly is expected to continue moving quickly toward the west through the rest of this week. Update : As of 5 a.m. EDT Friday , Dolly continued to be a minimum-strength tropical storm, with sustained winds of 40 mph.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 616, "text_sha256": "97919b84d4ed82c44a374ddcf433c731dbc0c091136b424da7c1574a3d86a2f6", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:36.917794+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:36.965767+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-08-27T18:03:32", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.571626+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_80e24cbd9cab3af00f5d", "record_id": "article_80e24cbd9cab3af0", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27082026/inside-clean-energy-rooftop-solar-sales", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27082026/inside-clean-energy-rooftop-solar-sales", "title_original": "Rooftop Solar Is Having a Rough One", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-27T13:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Rooftop solar installers feel like a dog that’s been repeatedly kicked. President Donald Trump has made solar more expensive—or at least slowed the long-term decline in costs—by imposing tariffs on imported photovoltaic panels and other parts. Trump also signed a measure last year that phased out the main federal tax credit for rooftop solar. The […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 352, "text_sha256": "2744a119dcb19a4df952df5867d345b367eaed3a5a815f26a08aa5aee6c0680e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:14.065290+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 8, "end": 13, "evidence": "Rooftop solar installers feel like a dog that’s been repeatedly kicked. President Donald Trump has made solar more expensive—or at least slowed the long-"}], "policy_tools": [{"id": "subsidy", "label_zh": "补贴与激励", "label_en": "Subsidies and incentives", "start": 315, "end": 325, "evidence": "s and other parts. Trump also signed a measure last year that phased out the main federal tax credit for rooftop solar. The […]"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:14.077060+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-08-27T13:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_daba9c23467ca8af7877", "record_id": "article_daba9c23467ca8af", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/a-leading-chinese-miner-of-mozambiques-heavy-sands-linked-to-environmental-destruction", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/08/a-leading-chinese-miner-of-mozambiques-heavy-sands-linked-to-environmental-destruction", "title_original": "A ‘leading’ Chinese miner of Mozambique’s heavy sands linked to environmental destruction", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-08-27T08:35:43+00:00", "source_text": "A sand mining operation along the coast of central Mozambique’s Zambezia Province decimated hundreds of hectares of mangroves in just a few years, a Mongabay investigation has found. The area is under the control of Mozambique Heavy Sand Company VIII, part-owned by the Jinan Yuxiao Group, an influential Chinese mining group claiming to hold more than […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 356, "text_sha256": "469cdec091c83f25e3a95c659555839846dccb113ffe00d26bab5ba7b44f878d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:10.010874+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MZ", "alpha3": "MOZ", "name_zh": "莫桑比克", "name_en": "Mozambique"}, {"alpha2": "CN", "alpha3": "CHN", "name_zh": "中华人民共和国", "name_en": "China"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "t