{"text_id": "text_4ceb5979194e537cc2f3", "record_id": "article_4ceb5979194e537c", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/18062026/countries-adopt-declaration-to-combat-illegal-fishing", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/18062026/countries-adopt-declaration-to-combat-illegal-fishing", "title_original": "How Shining a Light on Ships Could Help Solve Illegal Fishing", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-18T17:36:58+00:00", "source_text": "Mamadou Sarr remembers when an artisanal fisherman in Dakar only had to helm his wooden pirogue a single kilometer offshore to find a rich bounty of sardines and cuttlefish. For generations, Senegal’s near shore was the staging ground for a noble trade passed down from father to son. Today, as a result of industrial overfishing […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 333, "text_sha256": "ae48c7a590c1140b1b06c93bb794cb357e92181db25470a0b790559c2eff2d70", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:06.061736+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "SN", "alpha3": "SEN", "name_zh": "塞内加尔", "name_en": "Senegal"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "SN", "alpha3": "SEN", "name_zh": "塞内加尔", "name_en": "Senegal"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:06.123419+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-18T17:36:58", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "SN", "alpha3": "SEN", "name_zh": "塞内加尔", "name_en": "Senegal", "start": 191, "end": 198, "matched_text": "Senegal", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_5a5caa7b3e5043f2e364", "record_id": "article_5a5caa7b3e5043f2", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/16062026/emergency-drawdown-at-flaming-gorge-hits-its-recreation-economy", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/16062026/emergency-drawdown-at-flaming-gorge-hits-its-recreation-economy", "title_original": "Emergency Drawdown at Flaming Gorge Hits Its Recreation Economy", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-16T21:43:17+00:00", "source_text": "As campers with boats flocked to Buckboard Marina at the start of Memorial Day weekend, Tony Valdez was busy issuing refunds and repairing broken boat ramps. One older Green River man, who walked with two canes, left with his money refunded for the season after discovering he could not safely make it down to the […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 317, "text_sha256": "4340cbfaec65c17501fdbf460416b52a18e00b2b1c39a0a03fe896e481f56a42", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:07.512678+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:07.635890+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-16T21:43:17", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c95226a17402b0d9a50b", "record_id": "article_c95226a17402b0d9", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/teeming-with-turtles-cabo-verde-island-sees-80-fold-increase-in-nesting-loggerheads", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/teeming-with-turtles-cabo-verde-island-sees-80-fold-increase-in-nesting-loggerheads", "title_original": "Teeming with turtles: Cabo Verde island sees 80-fold increase in nesting loggerheads", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-16T16:36:44+00:00", "source_text": "In 2018, night patrol teams on Boa Vista, the third-largest island in the Cabo Verde archipelago, started noticing a change along the beaches: The loggerhead turtles were arriving in significantly larger numbers than usual. In previous years, each team, comprised of staff and volunteers from local conservation NGO Cabo Verde Natura 2000 (CVN2), encountered between […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 370, "text_sha256": "81ced75dc175e095f54aab48aee36a5d75a81c4130f8baee8989e6b52843c145", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.057378+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CV", "alpha3": "CPV", "name_zh": "佛得角", "name_en": "Cabo Verde"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CV", "alpha3": "CPV", "name_zh": "佛得角", "name_en": "Cabo Verde"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.099218+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-16T16:36:44", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CV", "alpha3": "CPV", "name_zh": "佛得角", "name_en": "Cabo Verde", "start": 22, "end": 32, "matched_text": "Cabo Verde", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "CV", "alpha3": "CPV", "name_zh": "佛得角", "name_en": "Cabo Verde", "start": 74, "end": 84, "matched_text": "Cabo Verde", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_a23394092d8aa3286e28", "record_id": "article_a23394092d8aa328", "canonical_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/energy/why-chinas-belt-and-road-oil-and-gas-boom-is-different-this-time", "publisher_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/energy/why-chinas-belt-and-road-oil-and-gas-boom-is-different-this-time", "title_original": "Why China’s Belt and Road oil-and-gas boom is different this time", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Dialogue Earth", "source_id": "INT009", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-16T15:23:10+00:00", "source_text": "In 2025, China’s engagement in countries signed up to the Belt and Road reached its highest level since the initiative’s launch, driven by a sharp uptick in oil and gas deals. Energy engagement, including both investment and construction contracts, reached USD 93.9 billion last year – more than double that of 2024, according to a report by the Green Finance and Development Center. Oil and gas alone accounted for roughly USD 71.5 billion of the total, tripling previous records and making up 74% of overseas energy engagement, the highest fossil-fuel share since 2014. While this macro-data appears to signal a major return to oil and gas, a closer look reveals a more nuanced structural shift.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 697, "text_sha256": "f4d23c290649f259bcc033acff45ed30b003c71001675b25285004a7efbd8f18", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:35.794492+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "93.9 billion", "start": 261, "end": 273, "evidence": " Energy engagement, including both investment and construction contracts, reached USD 93.9 billion last year – more than double that of 2024, according to a report by the Green Finance and Development Center.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}, {"value_text": "71.5 billion", "start": 428, "end": 440, "evidence": " Oil and gas alone accounted for roughly USD 71.5 billion of the total, tripling previous records and making up 74% of overseas energy engagement, the highest fossil-fuel share since 2014.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}, {"value_text": "74%", "start": 495, "end": 498, "evidence": "5 billion of the total, tripling previous records and making up 74% of overseas energy engagement, the highest fossil-fuel share since 2014.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CN", "alpha3": "CHN", "name_zh": "中华人民共和国", "name_en": "China"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 176, "end": 182, "evidence": "ghest level since the initiative’s launch, driven by a sharp uptick in oil and gas deals. Energy engagement, including both investment and construction contracts, reached USD 93.9 billion last year – more than double that of 2024, accor"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CN", "alpha3": "CHN", "name_zh": "中华人民共和国", "name_en": "China"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://dialogue.earth/en/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:35.827704+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-16T15:23:10", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CN", "alpha3": "CHN", "name_zh": "中华人民共和国", "name_en": "China", "start": 4, "end": 9, "matched_text": "China", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "CN", "alpha3": "CHN", "name_zh": "中华人民共和国", "name_en": "China", "start": 9, "end": 14, "matched_text": "China", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_74cc77d6529a1d5f1009", "record_id": "article_74cc77d6529a1d5f", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/beyond-wildlife-trade-endangered-pangolins-are-losing-habitat-in-pakistan", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/beyond-wildlife-trade-endangered-pangolins-are-losing-habitat-in-pakistan", "title_original": "Beyond wildlife trade: Endangered pangolins are losing habitat in Pakistan", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-16T13:22:55+00:00", "source_text": "Tariq Mahmood was alarmed when he found 19 sacks tucked away in a railway tunnel in the Chakwal district of northern Pakistan. Their contents were extremely disturbing: 45 rotting pangolin carcasses, all devoid of their distinct, orange-and-light-brown scales. That was in 2012. “It was very difficult to see these innocent, dead bodies,” said Mahmood, a […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 358, "text_sha256": "e92ba5446be354c6d26061dd18597b02e2516e5d049b705f61b4a28b9688ce64", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.137403+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.189068+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-16T13:22:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan", "start": 66, "end": 74, "matched_text": "Pakistan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan", "start": 117, "end": 125, "matched_text": "Pakistan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_9ff85b8195121d163540", "record_id": "article_9ff85b8195121d16", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/16062026/joint-base-andrews-piscataway-creek-fuel-leak-water-testing", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/16062026/joint-base-andrews-piscataway-creek-fuel-leak-water-testing", "title_original": "Months After a Jet Fuel Leak, No Agency Tested Waters Downstream of Piscataway Creek. So Community Groups Are Doing It Themselves.", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-16T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "In the five months after jet fuel started leaking from Joint Base Andrews into Piscataway Creek, no agency tested the water or sediment some 20 miles downstream, where the creek empties into the Potomac River and the shoreline community and anglers gather to fish and boat along the riverbank. The leak was detected on Dec. […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 327, "text_sha256": "bb6c91247b05e42cd2ab676845af3bb1248ce544c29dd5f3abd2f45c1ca52311", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:07.856779+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:07.916576+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-16T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_cb289ad3e0a708df9a18", "record_id": "article_cb289ad3e0a708df", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/plastic-food-packaging-blankets-the-worlds-coastlines-study-finds", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/plastic-food-packaging-blankets-the-worlds-coastlines-study-finds", "title_original": "Plastic food packaging blankets the world’s coastlines, study finds", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-15T16:12:01+00:00", "source_text": "Food packaging ranks among the top plastic pollutants littering the world’s coastlines, a new study confirms. The study, published May 20 in the journal One Earth, analyzed data from 112 nations, including 5,300 shoreline litter surveys, to produce the first global index of macroplastic pollution by usage type. Based on 355 peer-reviewed studies, it found […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 361, "text_sha256": "fbcf61bbfc81ff9838ccc13038b419de6cc7bd875a2dfca49f1689f37d5f360c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.762073+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.801269+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-15T16:12:01", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_09bb889c2f6ea61987d7", "record_id": "article_09bb889c2f6ea619", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/06/este-remolino-giratorio-genera-tormentas-como-le-afectara-el-cambio-climatico", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/06/este-remolino-giratorio-genera-tormentas-como-le-afectara-el-cambio-climatico", "title_original": "Este remolino giratorio genera tormentas. ¿Cómo le afectará el cambio climático?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-15T14:40:19+00:00", "source_text": "[Read in English here] En septiembre de 2024, intensas lluvias de más de ocho pulgadas (203 mm) cayeron en zonas de Centroamérica y el sur de México. Las lluvias, una señal de advertencia de lo que estaba por venir, fueron provocadas por un extenso sistema meteorológico de baja presión conocido como Giro Centroamericano , que se desarrolló sobre Centroamérica y las aguas adyacentes del Caribe, del Golfo de México y del Pacífico Oriental. Tras permanecer activo durante tres días, la porción del Giro Centroamericano situada sobre el noroeste del Caribe se separó de la baja principal y evolucionó hasta convertirse en el Huracán Helene, uno de los huracanes más notorios de la historia del Atlántico.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 704, "text_sha256": "bd46584d6ebe8f2dd7f1db703c99ad0932dadf1e4feb9e2b2f06d0775f5f3407", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:53.803739+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:45:53.824181+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-15T14:40:19", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_1667b64455ba8f25ffcc", "record_id": "article_1667b64455ba8f25", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/in-thailand-eudr-pressure-on-small-scale-rubber-farmers-prompts-private-sector-assistance", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/in-thailand-eudr-pressure-on-small-scale-rubber-farmers-prompts-private-sector-assistance", "title_original": "In Thailand, EUDR pressure on small-scale rubber farmers prompts private-sector assistance", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-15T02:02:31+00:00", "source_text": "KRABI, Thailand — Beneath a humid canopy of rubber trees, Sathit Phromraksa pauses to inspect a coagulated ball of rubber in a palm-sized bowl fastened to a trunk. Last night, he and his wife worked their way through the plantation, carefully carving a line in the bark of each tree to stimulate the flow of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 311, "text_sha256": "f096ce416161ac68154187b8b0a6198432bf0ac65e6969b50f76c355de2d3a25", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.888839+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "TH", "alpha3": "THA", "name_zh": "泰国", "name_en": "Thailand"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "TH", "alpha3": "THA", "name_zh": "泰国", "name_en": "Thailand"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:04.948845+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-15T02:02:31", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "TH", "alpha3": "THA", "name_zh": "泰国", "name_en": "Thailand", "start": 3, "end": 11, "matched_text": "Thailand", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "TH", "alpha3": "THA", "name_zh": "泰国", "name_en": "Thailand", "start": 7, "end": 15, "matched_text": "Thailand", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_a4bd618fea6f8a12180e", "record_id": "article_a4bd618fea6f8a12", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/tony-parkes-the-banker-who-replanted-a-rainforest", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/tony-parkes-the-banker-who-replanted-a-rainforest", "title_original": "Tony Parkes, the banker who replanted a rainforest", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-14T15:30:10+00:00", "source_text": "On the far north coast of New South Wales, the old rainforest had mostly disappeared. The Big Scrub once covered about 75,000 hectares of rich basalt country, a lowland subtropical forest of figs, vines, palms and fruit doves. By the time modern conservationists took stock of it, little more than one percent remained, divided among […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 337, "text_sha256": "7892c4b27b5a6ab7ff82ed2cf548ef7927b9c13e6beaa139e0204f009904486c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:14.453956+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "GB", "alpha3": "GBR", "name_zh": "英国", "name_en": "United Kingdom"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "GB", "alpha3": "GBR", "name_zh": "英国", "name_en": "United Kingdom"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_