{"text_id": "text_90fd26ee16ebb537cdbe", "record_id": "article_90fd26ee16ebb537", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/11062026/earths-massive-underground-fungal-networks", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/11062026/earths-massive-underground-fungal-networks", "title_original": "Threads of Earth’s Underground Fungal Networks Are Long Enough to Reach Beyond the Solar System", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-11T22:44:55+00:00", "source_text": "Hidden underground around the world lie 110 quadrillion kilometers of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungal networks—webs of ultra-thin threads that, if connected in a single line, would stretch almost a billion times the distance between the Earth and the sun, according to new research published in Science on Thursday. These fungal communities form intimate relationships with the […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 379, "text_sha256": "988f81af43263c32831fe7bd495d0bad4b785cd84ec4476a1e38806df7421644", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:10.441677+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:10.501932+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-11T22:44:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_cbce8a90dff7b41ef9b1", "record_id": "article_cbce8a90dff7b41e", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/10062026/rural-alabama-community-opposes-hyperscale-data-center", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/10062026/rural-alabama-community-opposes-hyperscale-data-center", "title_original": "On the Historic Route From Selma to Montgomery, an AI Cloud Looms", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-11T00:54:32+00:00", "source_text": "HAYNEVILLE, Ala.—When Alabamians marched from Selma to Montgomery in 1965 to demand voting rights for African Americans, Highway 80 became their path toward freedom. Two weeks after state troopers had violently attacked nonviolent demonstrators on that highway’s Edmund Pettus Bridge, Alabamians took back to the street. Led by Rev. Martin Luther King Jr., thousands of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 373, "text_sha256": "f64aaaf81d24a6f6b8d7a3e5fcf471a318447a8deb891a2eb75c900dac94bd54", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:11.190419+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:11.236814+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-06-11T00:54:32", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7e1719f8f9cdc7440f5e", "record_id": "article_7e1719f8f9cdc744", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/a-blueprint-for-effective-activism-10-years-after-defeating-a-dam-in-borneo-analysis", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/a-blueprint-for-effective-activism-10-years-after-defeating-a-dam-in-borneo-analysis", "title_original": "A blueprint for effective activism 10 years after defeating a dam in Borneo (analysis)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-06-10T18:59:56+00:00", "source_text": "In October 2015, Indigenous activists from Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Cambodia, Brazil, the United States, and Honduras, together with delegates from longhouse communities throughout the Malaysian state of Sarawak, gathered at Tanjung Tepalit, an Indigenous Kenyah village on the Baram River on the island of Borneo. They called the gathering WISER: the World Indigenous Summit […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 392, "text_sha256": "4c16b4a0b5a2584cedd8bfd8b1931bf478af304d7882d01a2e0c68bf09e42200", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:15.414809+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "PH", "alpha3": "PHL", "name_zh": "菲律宾", "name_en": "Philippines"}, {"alpha2": "MY", "alpha3": "MYS", "name_zh": "马来西亚", "name_en": "Malaysia"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_