{"text_id": "text_c4dbc331b6aaf320b31e", "record_id": "article_c4dbc331b6aaf320", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/a-good-year-for-forests-changes-less-than-it-seems", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/a-good-year-for-forests-changes-less-than-it-seems", "title_original": "A “good year” for forests changes less than it seems", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-29T17:55:31+00:00", "source_text": "The rate of tropical primary forest loss fell sharply in 2025, reversing the record highs of the year before. On paper, it looks like progress. In reality, the dip is likely only a temporary reprieve. The decline followed an exceptional year for wildfires. In 2024, drought helped drive some of the largest fire-related losses on […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 333, "text_sha256": "895d4e8018cd21354f9e0a4e3a0e6d5bfd75b82352f6f113fb4f583e1aaf0654", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.340475+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 246, "end": 254, "evidence": "the dip is likely only a temporary reprieve. The decline followed an exceptional year for wildfires. In 2024, drought helped drive some of the largest fire-related losses on […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.428583+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-29T17:55:31", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_54c3bb86c232bb5cc625", "record_id": "article_54c3bb86c232bb5c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/black-cockatoo-species-caught-in-the-crosshairs-of-global-race-for-minerals", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/black-cockatoo-species-caught-in-the-crosshairs-of-global-race-for-minerals", "title_original": "Black cockatoo species caught in the crosshairs of global race for minerals", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-29T14:06:38+00:00", "source_text": "Environmental organizations in southwest Australia have criticized the Australian government’s decision to grant the U.S. bauxite mining company Alcoa a national interest exemption, usually provided in cases of emergency, defense or national security, thereby authorizing the company to continue its operations despite years of unauthorized clearing in the country’s Northern Jarrah Forest. The Northern Jarrah […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 414, "text_sha256": "aaa78daeab067627a0a4ed79ff1148c3f1c709d6329cd95d7b7153ea6de3ca6d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.594522+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}, {"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 107, "end": 112, "evidence": "anizations in southwest Australia have criticized the Australian government’s decision to grant the U.S. bauxite mining company Alcoa a national interest exemption, usually provided in cases of emergency, defense or national security, "}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}, {"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.658727+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-29T14:06:38", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia", "start": 41, "end": 50, "matched_text": "Australia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 117, "end": 121, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_e4b1774a9ae6836b494f", "record_id": "article_e4b1774a9ae6836b", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/when-protest-works", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/when-protest-works", "title_original": "When protest works: Examples where activists have successfully pushed for change", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-28T01:11:29+00:00", "source_text": "Protest arrives with a clear sense of purpose. Annie Leonard and André Carothers avoid constructing a grand, unified theory of dissent and offer no rigid framework to explain why movements live or die. Instead, they have assembled a curated history: a series of episodes of resistance, each functioning as both narrative and instruction. The perspective […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 357, "text_sha256": "df0c3f7dcf72d569aeb120b595549c02b689abdecc2400531bf639b475fb3f5c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:03.278929+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:03.338855+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-28T01:11:29", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_06ad6a2f9626efe7e3cd", "record_id": "article_06ad6a2f9626efe7", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/heat-fires-and-agribusiness-squeeze-traditional-amazon-acai-harvesters", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/heat-fires-and-agribusiness-squeeze-traditional-amazon-acai-harvesters", "title_original": "Heat, fires and agribusiness squeeze traditional Amazon açaí harvesters", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-27T07:00:19+00:00", "source_text": "ACARÁ, Brazil — “I’ve spent my whole life working with açaí,” said Eliseu Carvalho, 57, who cultivates the berry in a floodplain area next to his home in the municipality of Acará, in the Brazilian state of Pará. “I’ve always made a living from it.” But after a devastating wildfire near his community, Carvalho is now considering abandoning açaí harvesting altogether. Acará is one of the most productive açaí regions in the state of Pará, with thousands of small-scale producers working in forest patches and along riverbanks. In 2024, the municipality was severely affected by an intense wildfire season. More than 18 million hectares (44.5 million acres) — an area the size of Cambodia — burned in the Amazon that year, according to the Brazilian collaborative research network MapBiomas .", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 793, "text_sha256": "3fbc703ba7baa037b4753b18cbf2984c211fdfe61a26ea313300e1adbe34963c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:13.095581+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quan