{"text_id": "text_3f25b49db355fc7736f4", "record_id": "article_3f25b49db355fc77", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/what-the-grim-outlook-for-alpine-ash-forests-tell-us-about-forestry-dogma-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/what-the-grim-outlook-for-alpine-ash-forests-tell-us-about-forestry-dogma-commentary", "title_original": "What the grim outlook for Alpine Ash forests tells us about forestry dogma (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-19T02:23:55+00:00", "source_text": "In March, the Australian Government announced that the Alpine Ash forests of mainland Australia have been listed as an Endangered Ecological Community under national environmental law. The Australian Government made the decision based on the recommendations of the independent Threatened Species Scientific Committee, although it has been opposed by logging lobby interests such as the […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 389, "text_sha256": "9e6a9fed3736c268150ce17aad8b5549dab41e5ec781da3327fc00b323d3848b", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:14.156541+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:14.177723+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-19T02:23:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "AU", "alpha3": "AUS", "name_zh": "澳大利亚", "name_en": "Australia", "start": 86, "end": 95, "matched_text": "Australia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_d18ef3ddf5176badffb8", "record_id": "article_d18ef3ddf5176bad", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/in-tasmania-the-mines-have-closed-but-the-rivers-remember", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/in-tasmania-the-mines-have-closed-but-the-rivers-remember", "title_original": "In Tasmania, the mines have closed but the rivers remember", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-16T21:17:55+00:00", "source_text": "The King River snakes through some of Tasmania’s most dramatic and diverse landscape, flowing past rainforest, button grass plains and the rugged peaks of the West Coast Range before emptying into a large bay near Strahan, a quiet fishing town. To the casual visitor, the winding stream looks as wild as the lightly settled country […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 335, "text_sha256": "449efc2eb2bb646859964fc1f031c1ab3fc800647b6af7e51f8e50719dbbc561", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.534977+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.555791+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-16T21:17:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_2272cef3c64188d98a5a", "record_id": "article_2272cef3c64188d9", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/listening-to-forests-reveals-signs-of-recovery-beyond-tree-cover", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/listening-to-forests-reveals-signs-of-recovery-beyond-tree-cover", "title_original": "Listening to forests reveals signs of recovery beyond tree cover", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-16T14:12:52+00:00", "source_text": "Can listening to forests help us understand if the life inside them is thriving? Apparently, yes. Giacomo Delgado likens it to a doctor examining heart health. “A doctor has listened to many people’s hearts, and knows what healthy hearts sound like,” Delgado, a doctoral researcher in the Department of Environmental Systems Science at ETH Zürich, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 351, "text_sha256": "9fe3cbd926787e2eda7cbabfcfef3bffa951bee9384c5fa624e511caa9396c47", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.650513+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.670793+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-16T14:12:52", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f2f7484a6e1f361fa5f7", "record_id": "article_f2f7484a6e1f361f", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-should-catalyze-african-biofertilizer-production-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-should-catalyze-african-biofertilizer-production-commentary", "title_original": "Strait of Hormuz crisis should catalyze African biofertilizer production (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-16T00:44:17+00:00", "source_text": "In early mornings across rural Kenya, as the long rains approach, farmers are already at work. Fields are being cleared, seeds checked, and planting plans quietly rehearsed. But this year, alongside the usual uncertainties about soil quality, rain and pests, there is a more pressing question: will there be enough fertilizer, and will it be […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 345, "text_sha256": "7bb77ec11d4cc410e049a9bcbdd5c986fce37d7a165d8c2f350a8d5687ef79ed", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.717889+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.736715+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-16T00:44:17", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya", "start": 31, "end": 36, "matched_text": "Kenya", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_30239819487e76ed3dee", "record_id": "article_30239819487e76ed", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/15042026/bronx-river-obsolete-dams-migratory-fish", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/15042026/bronx-river-obsolete-dams-migratory-fish", "title_original": "Dam Useless: Barriers Prevent a Migratory Fish from Reproducing", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-15T08:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "The Bronx River was once a curvy waterway that ran through vast forests and flowed into networks of tidal marshland. For centuries, river herring have swum up the waterway from the East River and the Long Island Sound to lay their eggs. But the river they traverse looks far different now. The waterway has been […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 315, "text_sha256": "af5dab9193a9d4a0d25f86ff4df3489e3a3b0d6799dc9f6b68ac47cf3a1340b3", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.417283+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:02.497402+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-04-15T08:55:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_bfe3b0a91fab6f3820ba", "record_id": "article_bfe3b0a91fab6f38", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/indonesia-braces-for-possible-godzilla-el-nino-as-fire-season-escalates-early", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/04/indonesia-braces-for-possible-godzilla-el-nino-as-fire-season-escalates-early", "title_original": "Indonesia braces for possible ‘Godzilla El Niño’ as fire season escalates early", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-04-15T04:12:41+00:00", "source_text": "JAKARTA — Indonesia is entering the 2026 fire season with early signs of escalation, as burned area surges even before the dry season peak and forecasts raise the possibility of a so-called “Godzilla” El Niño later this year. Burned area reached 32,637 hectares (80,650 acres) by February — about three times the size of Paris, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 331, "text_sha256": "b6e5269475cfb5ad0e938c910976bacbb283559664d1397460a8581031ffd0de", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:22.840929+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "annotation_