{"text_id": "text_d263880baa9fc0bbbdef", "record_id": "article_d263880baa9fc0bb", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/03/marine-flyways-are-the-missing-map-we-can-use-to-boost-seabird-conservation-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/03/marine-flyways-are-the-missing-map-we-can-use-to-boost-seabird-conservation-commentary", "title_original": "Marine flyways are the missing map we can use to boost seabird conservation (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-30T17:34:47+00:00", "source_text": "Last week, governments, conservationists and civil society from around the world gathered in Brazil for the 15th Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Migratory Species (CMS-15). In a rare moment of unity, they formally established something scientists have long understood but never before mapped at a global scale: marine flyways. This decision may […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 363, "text_sha256": "515247e59e530835d20b76366b1f013232923d26792098ae079022f695fbcaa7", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:37.271213+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:37.322731+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-30T17:34:47", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 93, "end": 99, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_86ecf98685e4ced1cbfc", "record_id": "article_86ecf98685e4ced1", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27032026/florida-data-center-costs-legislation", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/27032026/florida-data-center-costs-legislation", "title_original": "Legislation Aims to Protect Floridians From Data Center Costs, but Will It?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-27T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Legislation awaiting Gov. Ron DeSantis’ signature is aimed at ensuring hyper-scale data centers in Florida bear the full financial burden of powering their own facilities and that costs do not fall to average Floridians. The bill, approved by legislators earlier this month on the last day of their annual session, lays out the first regulations […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 349, "text_sha256": "e19c496c21d69a8d5e2b6c0ad1ff978f6849419e643374416e3e60d19463c4e2", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:17.170365+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "standards", "label_zh": "标准与监管", "label_en": "Standards and regulation", "start": 334, "end": 344, "evidence": "egislators earlier this month on the last day of their annual session, lays out the first regulations […]"}], "policy_stages": [{"id": "adopted", "label_zh": "通过", "label_en": "Adopted", "start": 231, "end": 239, "evidence": "powering their own facilities and that costs do not fall to average Floridians. The bill, approved by legislators earlier this month on the last day of their annual session, lays out the first regulations […]"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:17.229797+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-27T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_d8c4335af97fe9a210a0", "record_id": "article_d8c4335af97fe9a2", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/03/why-the-amazon-cant-be-saved-by-courts-alone-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/03/why-the-amazon-cant-be-saved-by-courts-alone-commentary", "title_original": "Why the Amazon can’t be saved by courts alone (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-26T18:32:22+00:00", "source_text": "In October 2023, a delegation of La Gente de Centro — the Andoke (Pɵɵsiɵhɵ), Nonuya (Nonova), Muinane (Féénemɨnaa) and Uitoto (Nɨpode) peoples of the Middle Caquetá River Basin — traveled from the Colombian Amazon to Bogotá. They came not as petitioners but as authorities of living territories, demanding the implementation of Supreme Court Ruling 4360 […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 357, "text_sha256": "4913076e96206f695de8026b0c3b264092167d312f1a7db2b0a037a74e1bd721", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:38.427186+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [{"id": "implementation", "label_zh": "实施", "label_en": "Implementation", "start": 310, "end": 324, "evidence": "otá. They came not as petitioners but as authorities of living territories, demanding the implementation of Supreme Court Ruling 4360 […]"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:38.488369+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-26T18:32:22", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f38e603574cf8d5d800f", "record_id": "article_f38e603574cf8d5d", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/25032026/epa-approves-higher-ethanol-blends-in-gasoline", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/25032026/epa-approves-higher-ethanol-blends-in-gasoline", "title_original": "As Prices Soar, EPA Greenlights Higher Ethanol Blends in Gasoline", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-25T23:52:51+00:00", "source_text": "The Trump administration handed farmers and the ethanol industry a win on Wednesday by issuing a waiver that will allow the use of higher corn-based ethanol blends in gas tanks this summer. Environmental Protection Agency Administrator Lee Zeldin made the announcement at CERAWeek, a major energy conference in Texas, saying it furthered the administration’s goal […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 367, "text_sha256": "553270d75814847e3f9e1bd64819a06030e5db150e0244fa2eb6ef2b71f0131f", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:17.756936+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 290, "end": 296, "evidence": "tal Protection Agency Administrator Lee Zeldin made the announcement at CERAWeek, a major energy conference in Texas, saying it furthered the administration’s goal […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:17.810811+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-25T23:52:51", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 311, "end": 316, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_9a4dabe7469a0698bccf", "record_id": "article_9a4dabe7469a0698", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/24032026/migratory-freshwater-fish-disappearing", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/24032026/migratory-freshwater-fish-disappearing", "title_original": "Earth’s Greatest Underwater Migrations Are Disappearing", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-24T12:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Beneath the surface of the planet’s rivers and lakes, the historically heaving migrations of freshwater fish are thinning out. The blubbery-lipped Siamese giant carp of Asia’s Mekong River, the mottled brown goonch of India’s Ganges and the ancient-in-appearance beluga sturgeon of Europe’s Danube River are declining. Facing existential threats along their migratory paths, an ecological […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 392, "text_sha256": "0d8867e7320957b5e00d6aabde151b688d87e6f6e8dbeadc641d78c24b6e53ce", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:18.222511+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:18.258959+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-24T12:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India", "start": 218, "end": 223, "matched_text": "India", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_4bfe2c688c7b842b3cd1", "record_id": "article_4bfe2c688c7b842b", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/03/retiring-farmers-find-a-new-way-to-pass-on-their-land", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2026/03/retiring-farmers-find-a-new-way-to-pass-on-their-land", "title_original": "Retiring farmers find a new way to pass on their land", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-24T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Transcript: Farmers often spend decades caring for their land. And when they retire, many hope to pass it on to others who will farm in an environmentally responsible way. Some are even willing to donate part or all of their land – or sell it at a discount – to keep it in good hands. Villa: “It’s not just the land that they’re protecting. They’re also trying to pass on this legacy of a farm that they’ve built.” Kristina Villa is cofounder of the Farmers Land Trust , a national nonprofit. Her group helps landowners transfer their land into communal nonprofit ownership. The land is then leased at affordable, long-term rates to new farmers who might otherwise struggle to buy land.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 686, "text_sha256": "2e8ba6ee45e1b35cca65a2c075244d135f1b3c991af61ebb506371d60542a337", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:19.480233+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:19.519047+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-24T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_b122f7bf68ba193b78c9", "record_id": "article_b122f7bf68ba193b", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/21032026/venezuela-offshore-wind-opportunity", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/21032026/venezuela-offshore-wind-opportunity", "title_original": "Yes, Venezuela Has a Ton of Oil—But Its Biggest Opportunity Is Offshore Wind", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-21T08:50:00+00:00", "source_text": "From our collaborating partner Living on Earth, public radio’s environmental news magazine, an interview by Jenni Doering with Paasha Mahdavi, an associate professor of political science at the University of California, Santa Barbara. Since the U.S. capture of President Nicolás Maduro in early January, there has been a lot of discussion about Venezuela’s massive oil […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 372, "text_sha256": "a1f1c2c08919a5915f090fbf594cd0bfabf2e65aacb418608f654c7365fe2f4e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:24.234504+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}, {"alpha2": "VE", "alpha3": "VEN", "name_zh": "委内瑞拉玻利瓦尔共和国", "name_en": "Venezuela"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}, {"alpha2": "VE", "alpha3": "VEN", "name_zh": "委内瑞拉玻利瓦尔共和国", "name_en": "Venezuela"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:24.263811+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-21T08:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "VE", "alpha3": "VEN", "name_zh": "委内瑞拉玻利瓦尔共和国", "name_en": "Venezuela", "start": 5, "end": 14, "matched_text": "Venezuela", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 208, "end": 218, "matched_text": "California", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "VE", "alpha3": "VEN", "name_zh": "委内瑞拉玻利瓦尔共和国", "name_en": "Venezuela", "start": 345, "end": 354, "matched_text": "Venezuela", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_b6b092dce60bd16ceb68", "record_id": "article_b6b092dce60bd16c", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20032026/georgia-electric-ratepayers-consumer-advocates", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20032026/georgia-electric-ratepayers-consumer-advocates", "title_original": "Georgia Hasn’t Had a Consumer Advocate for Electric Ratepayers for 18 Years", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-03-20T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Eighteen years after Georgia eliminated its consumer utility advocate, the fight to bring the office back recently resurfaced at a Senate hearing. “I’m frustrated,” Robert Baker told the state Senate’s Regulated Industries and Utilities Committee in February. “I have been frustrated for 15 years.” Baker has pushed to restore Georgia’s Consumer Utilities Counsel (CUC) since […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 379, "text_sha256": "ef5a91f181139b0a03dc9abbabefd68ea6b78a9cf5274f667253b6eb94eb747a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:24.630902+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:24.659674+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-03-20T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
