{"text_id": "text_6fa50cfacff5d131d015", "record_id": "article_6fa50cfacff5d131", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/02/local-communities-join-global-push-to-protect-european-arctic-us-peatlands", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/02/local-communities-join-global-push-to-protect-european-arctic-us-peatlands", "title_original": "Communities join global push to protect European, Arctic & US peatlands", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-02-05T16:55:38+00:00", "source_text": "After her father’s death, Bigga-Helena Magga and her sister were determined that their ancestral homeland, Alttokangas, a Sámi boreal forest and peatland in Finland’s Inari municipality, would not be turned into a commercial forestry operation. “We chose to take care and protect our inherited site located along the Ivalojoki river, which held great significance to […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 370, "text_sha256": "465e3b673409ae38ff1b2145e7c09e5a06851ead935f14bef8d5f0094fda89e7", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:20.619252+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}, {"alpha2": "FI", "alpha3": "FIN", "name_zh": "芬兰", "name_en": "Finland"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "FI", "alpha3": "FIN", "name_zh": "芬兰", "name_en": "Finland"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:20.681647+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-02-05T16:55:38", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 59, "end": 61, "matched_text": "US", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "FI", "alpha3": "FIN", "name_zh": "芬兰", "name_en": "Finland", "start": 157, "end": 164, "matched_text": "Finland", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f5a837524201f038892f", "record_id": "article_f5a837524201f038", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/02/successful-campaign-proves-ghanas-forests-are-worth-more-than-gold-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/02/successful-campaign-proves-ghanas-forests-are-worth-more-than-gold-commentary", "title_original": "Successful campaign proves Ghana’s forests are worth more than gold (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-02-05T16:19:25+00:00", "source_text": "On Dec. 10, 2025, Ghana’s government revoked one of the worst pieces of environmental legislation in our country’s history. The Environmental Protection (Mining in Forest Reserves) Regulations passed in 2022 opened up nearly 90% of Ghana’s forest reserves, including globally significant biodiversity areas, to mining. These forests, which cover more than 9 million hectares (22 […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 382, "text_sha256": "706a548e6d9e16eacfc9ebb6c455e637f31634556734614902a330dfb7be779d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:20.731483+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "90%", "start": 225, "end": 228, "evidence": " The Environmental Protection (Mining in Forest Reserves) Regulations passed in 2022 opened up nearly 90% of Ghana’s forest reserves, including globally significant biodiversity areas, to mining.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}, {"value_text": "9 million", "start": 356, "end": 365, "evidence": " These forests, which cover more than 9 million hectares (22 […]", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "GH", "alpha3": "GHA", "name_zh": "加纳", "name_en": "Ghana"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "standards", "label_zh": "标准与监管", "label_en": "Standards and regulation", "start": 181, "end": 191, "evidence": "lation in our country’s history. The Environmental Protection (Mining in Forest Reserves) Regulations passed in 2022 opened up nearly 90% of Ghana’s forest reserves, including globally significant biodiversity areas, to mining. These forest"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "GH", "alpha3": "GHA", "name_zh": "加纳", "name_en": "Ghana"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:20.797394+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-02-05T16:19:25", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "GH", "alpha3": "GHA", "name_zh": "加纳", "name_en": "Ghana", "start": 27, "end": 32, "matched_text": "Ghana", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "GH", "alpha3": "GHA", "name_zh": "加纳", "name_en": "Ghana", "start": 18, "end": 23, "matched_text": "Ghana", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f79898f82f7667405431", "record_id": "article_f79898f82f766740", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/05022026/inside-clean-energy-when-gas-stations-vanish", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/05022026/inside-clean-energy-when-gas-stations-vanish", "title_original": "Looking Ahead to When Gas Stations Vanish", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-02-05T14:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Sooner than you think, your city may be down to its last gas station, or, in large cities, the last few gas stations. They likely will be owned or heavily subsidized by the government because few businesses can be profitable selling a product whose demand is no longer growing. When will this happen? In regions […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 315, "text_sha256": "931ecb1d545a487aa71aaab3b0bff60ab4df2acdcf6183ddd5ee427be1c69910", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:53.652201+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "subsidy", "label_zh": "补贴与激励", "label_en": "Subsidies and incentives", "start": 155, "end": 161, "evidence": "ion, or, in large cities, the last few gas stations. They likely will be owned or heavily subsidized by the government because few businesses can be profitable selling a product whose demand is no longer growing. When will this happen? "}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:53.674491+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2026-02-05T14:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.572641+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_0e62d5c6f521ec459531", "record_id": "article_0e62d5c6f521ec45", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/04022026/north-carolina-hog-farm-violations", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/04022026/north-carolina-hog-farm-violations", "title_original": "A Troubled Hog Farm in Wayne County, North Carolina, Is Hit With a New String of Violations", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2026-02-04T09:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "FREMONT, N.C.—On a chilly afternoon in early January, Samantha Krop, the Neuse riverkeeper, and Taylor Register, a water quality specialist, trekked along a ditch near White Oaks Farm in Wayne County. They work for the nonprofit, Sound Rivers, and had received a tip that something was amiss. It hadn’t rained in two weeks, yet there […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 337, "text_sha256": "64985c2718ca7d08c87abc728450f959bd54dc9ff88e71917dfd3829cd224f49", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:54.018936+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_