{"text_id": "text_fa1258ee18c1f6e91589", "record_id": "article_fa1258ee18c1f6e9", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/12/respecting-uncontacted-peoples-can-protect-biodiversity-and-our-humanity-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/12/respecting-uncontacted-peoples-can-protect-biodiversity-and-our-humanity-commentary", "title_original": "Respecting uncontacted peoples can protect biodiversity and our humanity (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-12-03T21:17:10+00:00", "source_text": "Deep within the remaining tropical forests of the world, the last uncontacted peoples live in near-total isolation. Their very presence carries unintended yet powerful implications for all of us. Studies show that Indigenous territories — especially those of uncontacted groups — are among the least disturbed ecosystems on Earth. Protecting regions inhabited by uncontacted Indigenous […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 389, "text_sha256": "a6d661aa58b12ac5c80eb329b300b6b8c483df03141cd033fdb2dec9327b3e30", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:04.283995+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 214, "end": 224, "evidence": "ry presence carries unintended yet powerful implications for all of us. Studies show that Indigenous territories — especially those of uncontacted groups — are among the least disturbed ecosystems on Earth. Protecting regions inhabited by u"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:04.312894+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-12-03T21:17:10", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_73943469890ae5255379", "record_id": "article_73943469890ae525", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02122025/todays-climate-global-wildlife-trade-regulations-illegal", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02122025/todays-climate-global-wildlife-trade-regulations-illegal", "title_original": "As Countries Take Steps to Protect Wildlife in Legal Trade, Animal and Plant Trafficking Rages On", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-12-02T22:26:40+00:00", "source_text": "Whether people realize it or not, traces of the global wildlife trade are ubiquitous, from expensive reptile-skin boots in department stores to the colorful fish swimming around a tank in your dentist’s office. This multi-billion-dollar industry is regulated by a global treaty known as the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 364, "text_sha256": "95d6f6f5cb1ece48df3a477bce9034d8b550bff816646a360fa5128c043fa2d2", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:35.720679+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:35.743461+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-12-02T22:26:40", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_36287f95f34eb309219c", "record_id": "article_36287f95f34eb309", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/12/healthy-oceans-are-a-human-right-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/12/healthy-oceans-are-a-human-right-commentary", "title_original": "Healthy oceans are a human right (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-12-01T22:43:20+00:00", "source_text": "Months after a container ship went down off the coast of India, toxic pollution still contaminates the water and plastic pellets still wash ashore. Meanwhile, cleanup efforts continue, fishing restrictions remain, and legal claims crawl through the courts. When one shipwreck can unravel a season’s income or undermine health and public safety, it’s clear that […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 364, "text_sha256": "09be13bcd010d1c71f296df63356b67a52e4bedf6285c445fd2cb42339a6a432", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:04.482879+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:04.499401+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-12-01T22:43:20", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India", "start": 57, "end": 62, "matched_text": "India", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
