a multi-state effort to speed more electricity sources onto the grid. All but a handful of the"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:08.153375+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-18T08:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_8c65c28fe065d6cd304e", "record_id": "article_8c65c28fe065d6cd", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/17102025/public-lands-congressional-review-act-could-impact-other-states", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/17102025/public-lands-congressional-review-act-could-impact-other-states", "title_original": "Use of Congressional Review Act on BLM Plans Could Impact State Plans Under Other Agencies", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-10-17T22:34:50+00:00", "source_text": "After Republicans in the U.S. House of Representatives invoked the Congressional Review Act against Bureau of Land Management land-use plans last month, experts warned that similar future actions could potentially impact management plans in other states that fall under different federal agencies. In September, the House passed resolutions under the Congressional Review Act (CRA)—a little-known […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 400, "text_sha256": "59deea550808bd47cb4a4142a2c3a60af53f9e148bb222caf8580e10e11828aa", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:08.169120+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:08.182842+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-17T22:34:50", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 25, "end": 29, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_9afb05b14adc5c9ed04d", "record_id": "article_9afb05b14adc5c9e", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/17102025/jose-gualinga-kichwa-people-sarayaku-living-forest-declaration", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/17102025/jose-gualinga-kichwa-people-sarayaku-living-forest-declaration", "title_original": "How a Declaration of Ancestral Wisdom Is Changing Law, Science and Our Understanding of the World", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-10-17T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "When José Gualinga took the stage in a packed New York University law school auditorium in September, he admitted to feeling emotional. His audience had just watched the premiere of the documentary “Allpa Ukundi, Ñukanchi Pura” (Underground, Around and Among Us). The film showcases the Indigenous Kichwa People of Sarayaku and their pioneering efforts to […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 359, "text_sha256": "708b134888e06b24fd5e5da726cdcf7ac174a3410fccf715c762f44108704b6a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:08.326022+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 287, "end": 297, "evidence": " “Allpa Ukundi, Ñukanchi Pura” (Underground, Around and Among Us). The film showcases the Indigenous Kichwa People of Sarayaku and their pioneering efforts to […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:08.340360+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-17T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c4ba215fdf39b3aacc74", "record_id": "article_c4ba215fdf39b3aa", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/10/when-drought-meets-deluge", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/10/when-drought-meets-deluge", "title_original": "When drought meets deluge", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-10-16T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Transcript: It may seem counterintuitive, but some areas are suffering from both droughts and extreme rain. For example, in June and July, catastrophic floods devastated Texas Hill Country – a region that’s been experiencing drought for years. Lisonbee: “So we had, back to back, this extreme and prolonged drought that was then hit by these extreme and very intense floods.” Joel Lisonbee is with the Cooperative Institute for Research in Environmental Sciences at the University of Colorado, Boulder. He says a few torrential storms do not necessarily end a drought. After the storms in Texas … Lisonbee: “The grass greened up, the pastures improved, the soils became saturated again. But the long-term drought didn’t leave.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 726, "text_sha256": "160efc42e5b0b6ddb1c4c00be02b018cd649e84dad6cbfcc84240d0ae12c351a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:00.240014+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 81, "end": 88, "evidence": "Transcript: It may seem counterintuitive, but some areas are suffering from both droughts and extreme rain. For example, in June and July, catastrophic floods devastated Texas Hill Country – a region that’s been experiencing dro"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:00.288410+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-16T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 170, "end": 175, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f5d040d6a86e1f572fe3", "record_id": "article_f5d040d6a86e1f57", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/losing-nemo-in-the-red-sea-clownfish-vanish-as-anemones-bleach", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/losing-nemo-in-the-red-sea-clownfish-vanish-as-anemones-bleach", "title_original": "Losing Nemo: In the Red Sea, clownfish vanish as anemones bleach", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-10-14T20:16:33+00:00", "source_text": "When Morgan Bennett-Smith descended to a familiar reef in the central Red Sea in September 2023, he expected to find the same tagged anemones and resident clownfish he had been monitoring for months. Instead, he found a ghostly landscape: every anemone had turned white, and most of the bright-orange fish that had been sheltering in […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 337, "text_sha256": "2318842047f7c91766840c22c8b86081f79252e1768b47c1c4a47af875f31865", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:46.654282+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:46.668739+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-14T20:16:33", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_e47b44b3e2d741416317", "record_id": "article_e47b44b3e2d74141", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/in-indonesias-mentawai-islands-youths-blend-ancestral-and-world-faiths-to-protect-forests", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/in-indonesias-mentawai-islands-youths-blend-ancestral-and-world-faiths-to-protect-forests", "title_original": "In Indonesia’s Mentawai Islands, youths blend ancestral and world faiths to protect forests", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-10-14T15:53:47+00:00", "source_text": "Off the western coast of Sumatra, the Mentawai Islands rise from the Indian Ocean in a patchwork of emerald forests and winding rivers. The canopy shelters endemic macaques and gibbons, hornbills and orchids, while coastal villages still echo with rituals that tie people to the land and sea. Among the younger generation of Indigenous Mentawai, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 349, "text_sha256": "18a23a1aba2c73d55f2fd710b235c7873061821ba3f1cb0f6f1332b3ff248441", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:46.743679+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 325, "end": 335, "evidence": "ll echo with rituals that tie people to the land and sea. Among the younger generation of Indigenous Mentawai, […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:46.760266+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-10-14T15:53:47", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia", "start": 3, "end": 12, "matched_text": "Indonesia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
