{"text_id": "text_fbdf5adef00f9c8fd95c", "record_id": "article_fbdf5adef00f9c8f", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/24092025/deepfake-ai-whales-conservation-efforts", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/24092025/deepfake-ai-whales-conservation-efforts", "title_original": "Could These ‘Deepfake’ Whales Aid Conservation Efforts?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-24T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "It’s a hyper-modern problem on social media: A video or image of an animal doing something seemingly unbelievable in the wild pops up on your feed, only for you to realize it is, in fact, unbelievable. That’s because many of these images and videos—from wolves befriending house cats to brown bears jumping on a trampoline—are […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 330, "text_sha256": "1749d426e2b8051ed2caae8c852608cdd75914820cf75ce7d1c1cb89d4e9e316", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:28.068907+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:28.111907+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-24T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_eb8f42fbdbf56e1a1549", "record_id": "article_eb8f42fbdbf56e1a", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/ev-trial-among-bali-east-coast-fishers-shows-promise-amid-headwinds", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/ev-trial-among-bali-east-coast-fishers-shows-promise-amid-headwinds", "title_original": "EV trial among Bali east coast fishers shows promise amid headwinds", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-22T05:25:20+00:00", "source_text": "KLUNGKUNG, Indonesia — Many of the fishing boats here in Kusamba village leave behind the black sand in near silence as each jukung motors away from Bali’s east coast. “We’re on — it’s just not that loud,” boat captain Nengah Sudiarta told Mongabay Indonesia, his hand guiding the electric vehicle out from the Kusamba shoreline. […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 333, "text_sha256": "99c6fc89b8dd44f4282cdfc0d955c323a4abf7d0060eb70330ff82b71c7d5784", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:01.351796+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:01.365190+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-22T05:25:20", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia", "start": 11, "end": 20, "matched_text": "Indonesia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_851765e5454a78f78dfc", "record_id": "article_851765e5454a78f7", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/navigating-conservations-crisis", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/navigating-conservations-crisis", "title_original": "Navigating conservation’s crisis (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-21T13:23:16+00:00", "source_text": "Call it a crossroads. Ecological decline is accelerating in too many places at once; institutions that once limited the damage are wobbling; the information channels we rely on to coordinate action are clogged. In tropical forests alone, annual primary forest loss has climbed by 50% in the 2020s relative to the 2000s. Fires, drought and fragmentation have […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 361, "text_sha256": "b14a2035c5a8ef0a6c1016c0114224241145fe33d6ed70f269b74c9c961fb779", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:01.386583+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "50%", "start": 280, "end": 283, "evidence": " In tropical forests alone, annual primary forest loss has climbed by 50% in the 2020s relative to the 2000s.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 327, "end": 334, "evidence": " annual primary forest loss has climbed by 50% in the 2020s relative to the 2000s. Fires, drought and fragmentation have […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:01.399010+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-21T13:23:16", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_a490d42126fc95116960", "record_id": "article_a490d42126fc9511", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20092025/west-union-geothermal-energy-network", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20092025/west-union-geothermal-energy-network", "title_original": "This Town Was One of the First in the Nation to Install a Geothermal Network. Now Others Are Warming Up to the Idea.", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-20T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "WEST UNION, Iowa—From the billboard on the edge of town to the limestone monument on Vine Street, the signs are hard to miss: “West Union, Deeply Connected.” It’s a motto that could apply to many tight-knit farm towns across the Midwest where families date back generations. But in this town of 2,500, the words have […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 320, "text_sha256": "d2518a3b9a0a0eb1197211daffdc9a42572f637ed9dac87c95a015df8e95b957", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:29.895808+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:29.937339+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-20T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_acfa94f060fd874c3522", "record_id": "article_acfa94f060fd874c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/the-formula-that-reduced-deforestation-in-brazil-in-the-21st-century", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/the-formula-that-reduced-deforestation-in-brazil-in-the-21st-century", "title_original": "The formula that reduced deforestation in Brazil in the 21st century", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-19T09:26:59+00:00", "source_text": "The dramatic reduction in deforestation in Brazil between 2004 and 2012 was the result of an ‘all of government approach’, which was closely coordinated with private initiatives responding to international boycotts that targeted commodity supply chains. Launched in the first year of President Inácio Lula da Silva’s first term, the Action Plan for the Prevention […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 367, "text_sha256": "aca4d7341e8ae2940560184d22f46b3634cca50755207f26fb968d9574179f90", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:06.729945+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:06.743471+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-19T09:26:59", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 42, "end": 48, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 43, "end": 49, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_b374e4f3a7fef9dae1ec", "record_id": "article_b374e4f3a7fef9da", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/19092025/north-carolina-cattle-farmer-fined", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/19092025/north-carolina-cattle-farmer-fined", "title_original": "North Carolina Cattle Farmer to Pay $92,000 for Damaging Mountain Streams", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-19T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "ALLEGHANY COUNTY, N.C.—One of the most prominent cattle farmers in North Carolina has reached a financial settlement with the state Department of Environmental Quality over allegations that its grazing operations damaged more than three miles of mountain streams and prompted state wildlife officials to conduct an emergency rescue of a fragile species of brook trout […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 371, "text_sha256": "71fcaadbcaee7c38782ca47ef6620848506b6376a3e7273438f47b47fa57d6e6", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:30.735642+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "ar