{"text_id": "text_2efbc87a8ff447c99845", "record_id": "article_2efbc87a8ff447c9", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/new-report-recommends-ways-to-increase-womens-access-to-funding", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/new-report-recommends-ways-to-increase-womens-access-to-funding", "title_original": "New report recommends ways to increase women’s access to funding", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-05T07:00:07+00:00", "source_text": "A new report, published ahead of the International Day of Indigenous Women on Sept. 5, analyzed structural barriers faced by Indigenous, Afro-descendant and other local community women’s organizations in accessing funding for conservation, land rights and gender equality projects — and it offers several recommendations to address these challenges. “When women have secure land and […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 386, "text_sha256": "e0588bab237099ff10896b6aba742b9ea8da3e65e55c1112ff10e9b109d97141", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.468034+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 58, "end": 68, "evidence": "A new report, published ahead of the International Day of Indigenous Women on Sept. 5, analyzed structural barriers faced by Indigenous, Afro-descendant and other local community women’s organizations in acce"}], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 214, "end": 221, "evidence": " Indigenous, Afro-descendant and other local community women’s organizations in accessing funding for conservation, land rights and gender equality projects — and it offers several recommendations to address these challenges. “When women"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.480633+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-05T07:00:07", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_59f044f1ea8d722e65e5", "record_id": "article_59f044f1ea8d722e", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/eudr-implementation-comes-laden-with-potential-unintended-consequences", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/eudr-implementation-comes-laden-with-potential-unintended-consequences", "title_original": "EUDR implementation comes laden with potential unintended consequences", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-04T19:05:51+00:00", "source_text": "Set to enter into force Dec. 30, 2025, the European Union’s deforestation-free products regulation (EUDR) aims to halt the bloc’s contribution to global forest loss. Experts Mongabay spoke to agree the EUDR promises to become a landmark legislative tool for curbing commodities supply chain-related deforestation at the international level. But those analysts also warn of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 376, "text_sha256": "a9f5242aaeb0909760288f3205f7477169a0d6566cade9d749770fba11b8e5e6", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.516133+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "standards", "label_zh": "标准与监管", "label_en": "Standards and regulation", "start": 88, "end": 98, "evidence": "Set to enter into force Dec. 30, 2025, the European Union’s deforestation-free products regulation (EUDR) aims to halt the bloc’s contribution to global forest loss. Experts Mongabay spoke to agree the EUDR promises to become a landmark l"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.529264+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-04T19:05:51", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_91a5ebe47395914d1326", "record_id": "article_91a5ebe47395914d", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/report-sees-20b-in-revenue-for-amazon-redd-projects-despite-unmet-promises", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/report-sees-20b-in-revenue-for-amazon-redd-projects-despite-unmet-promises", "title_original": "Report sees $20B in revenue for Amazon REDD+ projects despite unmet promises", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-04T14:03:13+00:00", "source_text": "A new report by the Earth Innovation Institute (EII) estimates that REDD+ jurisdictional projects in the Brazilian Amazon could generate up to $20 billion through the sale of carbon credits. The study also projects that, if fully implemented, these programs could accelerate forest protection measures and reduce deforestation by up to 90% by 2030. The report was commissioned with an openly optimistic approach, according to one of the authors, as a way to counterpoint recent warnings that the Amazon is approaching a tipping point and may be losing its capacity as a carbon sink. “We want to show another side to the ‘point of no return’ argument,” Daniel Nepstad, lead author and president of EII, told Mongabay.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 716, "text_sha256": "64b0fc81eb002cef877143be22c722459846b6578426e34896521fb2f7704dff", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.555578+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "$20 billion", "start": 143, "end": 154, "evidence": "A new report by the Earth Innovation Institute (EII) estimates that REDD+ jurisdictional projects in the Brazilian Amazon could generate up to $20 billion through the sale of carbon credits.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}, {"value_text": "90%", "start": 336, "end": 339, "evidence": " The study also projects that, if fully implemented, these programs could accelerate forest protection measures and reduce deforestation by up to 90% by 2030.", "interpretation": "target_or_commitment"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "carbon_markets", "label_zh": "碳市场", "label_en": "Carbon markets", "start": 175, "end": 188, "evidence": "nal projects in the Brazilian Amazon could generate up to $20 billion through the sale of carbon credits. The study also projects that, if fully implemented, these programs could accelerate forest protection measures and reduce deforestation b"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [{"id": "implementation", "label_zh": "实施", "label_en": "Implementation", "start": 230, "end": 241, "evidence": "to $20 billion through the sale of carbon credits. The study also projects that, if fully implemented, these programs could accelerate forest protection measures and reduce deforestation by up to 90% by 2030. The report was commissioned with"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.572367+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-04T14:03:13", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_dc797165c5b26c74e5eb", "record_id": "article_dc797165c5b26c74", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/the-making-of-an-autonomous-indigenous-nation-in-peru", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/09/the-making-of-an-autonomous-indigenous-nation-in-peru", "title_original": "The making of an autonomous Indigenous nation in Peru’s Amazon", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-03T17:19:55+00:00", "source_text": "In 2015, leaders of the Wampís did what no other Indigenous peoples have done in Peru’s modern history: They declared themselves an autonomous nation to gain greater control over their territory. For decades, the Indigenous Wampís (or Huambisa) of the northern Peruvian Amazon have protested against oil drilling and other extractive activities in their home, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 363, "text_sha256": "63b1d8d50ddaf6098b068fa6722687ae9bc51e2ce42c972b98f083c6afc68473", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.582165+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "PE", "alpha3": "PER", "name_zh": "秘鲁", "name_en": "Peru"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 49, "end": 59, "evidence": "In 2015, leaders of the Wampís did what no other Indigenous peoples have done in Peru’s modern history: They declared themselves an autonomous nation to gain greater control over their territory. For"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "PE", "alpha3": "PER", "name_zh": "秘鲁", "name_en": "Peru"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.593943+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-03T17:19:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "PE", "alpha3": "PER", "name_zh": "秘鲁", "name_en": "Peru", "start": 49, "end": 53, "matched_text": "Peru", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "PE", "alpha3": "PER", "name_zh": "秘鲁", "name_en": "Peru", "start": 81, "end": 85, "matched_text": "Peru", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_974c8bf7c02d36fae8a1", "record_id": "article_974c8bf7c02d36fa", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03092025/arizona-border-wall-expansion-will-impact-wildlife", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03092025/arizona-border-wall-expansion-will-impact-wildlife", "title_original": "Activists Decry New Border Wall’s Impact on Wildlife", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-09-03T08:50:00+00:00", "source_text": "This story was originally published by National Catholic Reporter. TUCSON, Ariz.—The Trump administration is muscling forward with plans to wall off a critical international wildlife corridor, setting up construction camps to erect a 30-foot barrier along one of the few remaining gaps on the U.S.-Mexico border. The first of the steel bollards are expected to go up […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 370, "text_sha256": "6e6759699722adeb5110d026e8f07a2ec2827c58c6b20abf9710f2ff7bd00a12", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:48.595814+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 330, "end": 335, "evidence": "t barrier along one of the few remaining gaps on the U.S.-Mexico border. The first of the steel bollards are expected to go up […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:48.608538+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-09-03T08:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 293, "end": 297, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 298, "end": 304, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_e232d3507f53caf3fd4c", "record_id": "article_e232d3507f53caf3", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/30082025/trump-administration-roadless-rule-public-comment", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/30082025/trump-administration-roadless-rule-public-comment", "title_original": "The Trump Administration Is Trying to Revoke the ‘Roadless Rule.’ The Public Won’t Have Much Time to Weigh In", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-30T08:50:00+00:00", "source_text": "The U.S. Department of Agriculture is giving the public just three weeks to weigh in on a key step of its attempt to scrap the Roadless Rule, which protects almost 59 million acres of forest land from road construction and timber harvesting. The U.S. Forest Service (USFS) published a notice Friday seeking comment on its […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 325, "text_sha256": "aebaad74390276e3bacf3d9a4039d8e38b7ba44b578b83758844a15ee250112f", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:48.987491+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "59 million", "start": 164, "end": 174, "evidence": " Department of Agriculture is giving the public just three weeks to weigh in on a key step of its attempt to scrap the Roadless Rule, which protects almost 59 million acres of forest land from road construction and timber harvesting.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:49.001775+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-30T08:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 4, "end": 8, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_23376162c00db9c3bb5c", "record_id": "article_23376162c00db9c3", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/carbon-offset-markets-are-unfair-to-indigenous-communities-in-borneo-beyond-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/carbon-offset-markets-are-unfair-to-indigenous-communities-in-borneo-beyond-commentary", "title_original": "Carbon offset markets are unfair to communities in Borneo & beyond (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-29T19:14:30+00:00", "source_text": "I write this while waiting for my tablet to die. Tomorrow, I’ll return to air-conditioning, stable WiFi and refrigeration, but here in Long Moh, deep in the remote Upper Baram region of Sarawak, there has been no electricity for two weeks. The fans sit useless and mocking in the corners, and a sudden downpour is […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 317, "text_sha256": "11f69da02f449ff25df3b7c8a5cd64b9b657d911173510d9cbd5afd50e5f00e2", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:12.909448+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-j