{"text_id": "text_b0d31f95f54dc5801449", "record_id": "article_b0d31f95f54dc580", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/19082025/todays-climate-ghost-boats-pollution-waterways", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/19082025/todays-climate-ghost-boats-pollution-waterways", "title_original": "Supercharged Hurricanes Mean More ‘Ghost Boats’ Haunting Waterways", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-19T11:58:56+00:00", "source_text": "For nearly three years, drivers on San Carlos Island in Florida passed by an unusual sight tangled in the mangroves on the shoulder of a major road: a large white boat. The abandoned vessel was a relic of 2022’s Hurricane Ian, which displaced more than 7,000 vessels amid severe winds, torrential downpour and catastrophic storm […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 332, "text_sha256": "ca88ec15f14b0b61b096060d8d61f9fdf502edf28c0eeb9a36496b5217ea0ce2", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:55.615353+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:55.632911+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-19T11:58:56", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7fdbb24d0d96884fc2c0", "record_id": "article_7fdbb24d0d96884f", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/amazon-jambu-blends-tradition-and-science-for-numbing-flavors-and-healthcare", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/amazon-jambu-blends-tradition-and-science-for-numbing-flavors-and-healthcare", "title_original": "Amazon jambu blends tradition and science for numbing flavors and healthcare", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-18T14:34:48+00:00", "source_text": "The jambu plant is native to the Amazon Rainforest, where it’s renowned for its numbing and tingling effect when eaten. This characteristic has made it a main ingredient in many northern Brazilian dishes and drinks , as well as a traditional remedy for Indigenous communities living in Amazonian areas. But the benefits of the plant, Acmella oleracea , go even further: boosted by new studies, it’s now becoming a key ingredient of Brazil’s growing bioeconomy, thanks to researchers’ ability to turn local biodiversity and traditional knowledge into sustainable products with a huge socioeconomic impact. One of the initiatives is led by scientists from the Supercritical Technology Laboratory ( Labtecs ) at the Federal University of Pará (UFPA).", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 747, "text_sha256": "3462a128a11a40b62794577b8b7f53614c3643692fcdeb145dc2dcfc162e8e1a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:24.832661+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 253, "end": 263, "evidence": "edient in many northern Brazilian dishes and drinks , as well as a traditional remedy for Indigenous communities living in Amazonian areas. But the benefits of the plant, Acmella oleracea , go even further: boosted by new studies, it’s now "}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:24.895395+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-18T14:34:48", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 432, "end": 438, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f729200538586bb03c50", "record_id": "article_f729200538586bb0", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/argentina-pushes-pipeline-exports-through-protected-patagonian-waters", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/08/argentina-pushes-pipeline-exports-through-protected-patagonian-waters", "title_original": "Argentina pushes pipeline exports through protected Patagonian waters", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-18T13:32:55+00:00", "source_text": "San Matías Gulf, on the northern coast of Argentina’s Patagonia region, is one of the most biodiverse areas in the Argentine Sea. The Valdés Peninsula — a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1999 and a biosphere reserve since 2014 — forms its southern border. It’s surrounded by Islote Lobos National Park, the Puerto Lobos and […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 328, "text_sha256": "aa45bef48f7176b9d1ab9521f2d7bdd1112aba432d3dc51c8fec3622bad30658", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:25.045273+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "AR", "alpha3": "ARG", "name_zh": "阿根廷", "name_en": "Argentina"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "AR", "alpha3": "ARG", "name_zh": "阿根廷", "name_en": "Argentina"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:25.101729+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-18T13:32:55", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "AR", "alpha3": "ARG", "name_zh": "阿根廷", "name_en": "Argentina", "start": 0, "end": 9, "matched_text": "Argentina", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "AR", "alpha3": "ARG", "name_zh": "阿根廷", "name_en": "Argentina", "start": 42, "end": 51, "matched_text": "Argentina", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_8242b245103f1a163715", "record_id": "article_8242b245103f1a16", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/08/erin-vaults-from-tropical-storm-to-category-5-hurricane-in-just-25-hours", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/08/erin-vaults-from-tropical-storm-to-category-5-hurricane-in-just-25-hours", "title_original": "Erin vaults from tropical storm to Category 5 hurricane in just 25 hours", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-16T20:16:57+00:00", "source_text": "Strengthening at a jaw-dropping pace, Hurricane Erin – which had reached Category 1 strength at 11 a.m. EDT Friday, August 15 – was officially proclaimed a Category 5 storm at 11:20 a.m. EDT Saturday. As of 2 p.m. EDT Saturday , Erin’s top sustained winds were at 160 mph. Erin is the earliest cat 5 storm ever recorded in the open Atlantic (the area north and east of the Caribbean and Gulf of Mexico), and it’s one of the Atlantic’s fastest-strengthening storms on record. Erin was located about 110 miles north of Antigua, moving just north of due west at 16 mph. Erin’s central pressure was 915 mb. Update: After weakening to cat 3 strength early Sunday, the result of an eyewall replacement cycle, Erin reintensified as a larger hurricane later in the day. As of 2 a.m.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 774, "text_sha256": "80bb7b465d82c33089b276bf2e56d421650767c836db2ca3c9adadc6d7ddbf46", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:22.984029+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:23.201495+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-16T20:16:57", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 395, "end": 401, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_a4a271901c630fc90fb7", "record_id": "article_a4a271901c630fc9", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/15082025/chicago-air-pollution-sensors", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/15082025/chicago-air-pollution-sensors", "title_original": "Chicago Aims To Have Most Air Pollution Sensors in the US", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-15T08:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "City officials are scrambling to install nearly 300 high-quality air pollution sensors across Chicago, a network that would be the largest in the U.S. and one of the biggest worldwide. The plan is to have the monitors up by the end of summer as city officials try to get a handle on the poor air […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 299, "text_sha256": "39041bc9d85bb6bbad624374243f45a11da8204e1570625767cfefe61c2aff6b", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:56.794269+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:56.821667+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-08-15T08:55:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 55, "end": 57, "matched_text": "US", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 146, "end": 150, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.573678+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_5e3840cf1ce90ae21098", "record_id": "article_5e3840cf1ce90ae2", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/08/erin-gains-strength-in-the-atlantic", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/08/erin-gains-strength-in-the-atlantic", "title_original": "Erin gains strength in the Atlantic", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-08-14T19:24:40+00:00", "source_text": "[Haz clic aquí para leer en español] Tropical Storm Erin was steadily intensifying in the central tropical Atlantic on Thursday, en route for what may be a textbook route through the northwest Atlantic over the following week. Although there’s a chance Erin will avoid striking any land areas, many coastal areas will be plagued for […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 336, "text_sha256": "9894fce7e62e4713ebb8c68e79b2205788eb7021b392f5f13f6a77bdd7de1d80", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:30.434381+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:30.491685+00:00", "publi