{"text_id": "text_322f413d22bf9c21ea0c", "record_id": "article_322f413d22bf9c21", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/06/when-our-oceans-cant-breathe-a-sea-change-is-needed-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/06/when-our-oceans-cant-breathe-a-sea-change-is-needed-commentary", "title_original": "When our oceans can’t breathe, a sea change is needed (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-06-09T15:52:40+00:00", "source_text": "When wildfires rage across landscapes, smoke fills our skies and chokes our lungs. It makes headlines, emergency measures are triggered, and communities rally to respond. We act because we can see it, smell it, and feel it. But beneath the ocean’s surface, another crisis is silently unfolding. What happens when our oceans — the planet’s […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 342, "text_sha256": "5de9488bf1407a40782f822dc30271927a60bb55b3651c82606cdc28acac2141", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:03.760037+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 5, "end": 13, "evidence": "When wildfires rage across landscapes, smoke fills our skies and chokes our lungs. It makes headlines, emergency measures are triggered, and communities "}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:03.788033+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-06-09T15:52:40", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_3317adb74fd9b9495a09", "record_id": "article_3317adb74fd9b949", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06062025/todays-climate-community-science-inaturalist-merlin-science", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06062025/todays-climate-community-science-inaturalist-merlin-science", "title_original": "People Using Apps Like iNaturalist and Merlin Are Helping Fuel Scientific Discovery", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-06-06T20:06:07+00:00", "source_text": "In April, more than 100,000 people from nearly 700 cities around the world set out on a mission to document as many plants and animals as they could in their urban environments. The early results from this effort are in: Participants made more than 3.3 million observations of over 73,000 species, thousands of which are […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 324, "text_sha256": "45b0c600aa6a9dc8cd12ef0b8c7bd587ec78519134e6e2a6788bb9f7338dc636", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:42.506069+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "3.3 million", "start": 249, "end": 260, "evidence": " The early results from this effort are in: Participants made more than 3.3 million observations of over 73,000 species, thousands of which are […]", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:42.523299+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-06-06T20:06:07", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_fa801e825e9c51c839cb", "record_id": "article_fa801e825e9c51c8", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/06/como-afectan-el-sargazo-y-el-polvo-del-sahara-a-la-temporada-de-huracanes", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/06/como-afectan-el-sargazo-y-el-polvo-del-sahara-a-la-temporada-de-huracanes", "title_original": "¿Cómo afectan el sargazo y el polvo del Sahara a la temporada de huracanes?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-06-06T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "La temporada de huracanes en el Atlántico comenzó oficialmente el 1 de junio y se extenderá hasta el 30 de noviembre de 2025. Según los pronósticos de la Administración Nacional Oceánica y Atmosférica (NOAA), se espera una temporada más activa de lo normal, con entre 13 y 19 tormentas con nombre, de las cuales 6 a 10 podrían convertirse en huracanes, y entre 3 y 5 alcanzarían la categoría de huracanes mayores (categoría 3 o superior).", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 438, "text_sha256": "20ced43c15d3ab696b2c604ef9751222603d7dcd6392de79d4a3e168bc3950fb", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:49.471137+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:49.523223+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-06-06T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_6ef5481fae2d811930ac", "record_id": "article_6ef5481fae2d8119", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06062025/nantucket-sea-level-rise-coastal-resilience", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06062025/nantucket-sea-level-rise-coastal-resilience", "title_original": "How Nantucket Is Preparing for Rising Seas", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-06-06T08:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "NANTUCKET—It’s no longer unusual to see a kayaker paddling along downtown Easy Street. The cobblestones along the town’s waterfront once were flooded a handful of times a year. That rose to an average of 37 days a year by 2020, according to tide gauge monitors by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. The next year, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 335, "text_sha256": "360da9373dc0497d1c3526bb0671731794609bdb32c0aef3f7d68d3f6b246401", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:42.650668+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 142, "end": 147, "evidence": "ddling along downtown Easy Street. The cobblestones along the town’s waterfront once were flooded a handful of times a year. That rose to an average of 37 days a year by 2020, according to tide gauge monitors by the National Oceanic an"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:42.674577+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-06-06T08:55:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7377575168b6da1cc1c8", "record_id": "article_7377575168b6da1c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/06/unnoticed-oil-gas-threat-looms-for-indigenous-people-near-amazon-blocks", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/06/unnoticed-oil-gas-threat-looms-for-indigenous-people-near-amazon-blocks", "title_original": "Unnoticed oil & gas threat looms for Indigenous people near Amazon blocks", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-06-06T07:00:15+00:00", "source_text": "While oil prospects in the Amazon north shore attract international attention, the offer of exploration blocks around Indigenous territories goes unnoticed in Mato Grosso state.", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 177, "text_sha256": "cd28f15fdd4ab7415b1db8e8f6d25f990639a74fe389bd17fc458ce8b858bf4f", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:04.164170+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "justice", "label_zh": "公正转型", "label_en": "Just transition", "start": 118, "end": 128, "evidence": "mazon north shore attract international attention, the offer of exploration blocks around Indigenous territories goes unnoticed in Mato Grosso state."}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extrac