{"text_id": "text_e09f10db58819ee129d8", "record_id": "article_e09f10db58819ee1", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/tropical-storm-alvin-forms-off-the-pacific-coast-of-mexico", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/tropical-storm-alvin-forms-off-the-pacific-coast-of-mexico", "title_original": "Tropical Storm Alvin forms off the Pacific coast of Mexico", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-29T17:02:39+00:00", "source_text": "The first named storm of the 2025 eastern Pacific hurricane season, Tropical Storm Alvin, is gathering strength in the warm waters about 700 miles offshore of southwestern Mexico. Alvin formed at 11 a.m. EDT on Thursday, May 29, and it is poised to intensify into a moderate-strength tropical storm with 60 mph winds on Friday before wind shear and dry air reduce it to a remnant low over the weekend, before Alvin reaches the coast of Mexico. No watches or warnings are posted for Mexico.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 489, "text_sha256": "4421ac85d8b729cd5d8b102c316a6f6ba46df6d8cee4ec21f61e32daa58bd2d3", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:50.296759+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:50.328160+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-29T17:02:39", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 52, "end": 58, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 172, "end": 178, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_a42b3a77d0258ef9e10c", "record_id": "article_a42b3a77d0258ef9", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/hurricane-season-is-upon-us-but-noaa-and-fema-are-not-ready", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/hurricane-season-is-upon-us-but-noaa-and-fema-are-not-ready", "title_original": "Hurricane season is upon us, but NOAA and FEMA are not ready", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-28T14:32:30+00:00", "source_text": "Hurricane season starts June 1, and above-average activity is predicted . But America’s premier agencies for protecting lives and property from these destructive storms – the National Atmospheric and Oceanic Administration, or NOAA, and the Federal Emergency Management Association, or FEMA – are in unprecedented disarray. The chaos will likely harm hurricane forecast accuracy in 2025, as well as disaster preparation and response. NOAA reeling from huge staffing losses Massive staffing losses at NOAA from firings of probationary employees, DOGE buyouts, and early retirements have left at least eight of the 122 National Weather Service offices unable to operate around the clock.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 685, "text_sha256": "cae93c9ae9dac43853579c7031f4d1fb93c856a2ace64bbe7caafbbbfc63588b", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:50.362447+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:50.387810+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-28T14:32:30", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_bedd2697d0fba4d7a09a", "record_id": "article_bedd2697d0fba4d7", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/tuna-fishing-devices-drift-through-a-third-of-oceans-harming-corals-coasts-study", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/tuna-fishing-devices-drift-through-a-third-of-oceans-harming-corals-coasts-study", "title_original": "Tuna fishing devices drift through a third of oceans, harming corals, coasts: Study", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-28T07:03:53+00:00", "source_text": "A recent study reveals that drifting fish aggregating devices (dFADs), widely used in tuna fishing, have spread to more than a third of the world’s oceans. These devices harm ocean life and coastal communities, but weak rules and lack of accountability make it hard to manage them properly, some conservationists say. The study, published in […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 345, "text_sha256": "c9bb3940a8fc0e2b5656ea80f9b7248007e1f7ee5c847cc7cd1228667f22819a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.642964+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.658045+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-28T07:03:53", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_3ab5710b1abf371f844a", "record_id": "article_3ab5710b1abf371f", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/in-pakistan-desert-irrigation-plans-spark-protests-fears-among-sindh-farmers", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/in-pakistan-desert-irrigation-plans-spark-protests-fears-among-sindh-farmers", "title_original": "In Pakistan, desert irrigation plans spark protests & fears among Sindh farmers", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-28T03:00:39+00:00", "source_text": "On April 6, Wajahat Hussain, a Sindhi human rights lawyer, spoke at a protest against the planned Cholistan Canal Project on the Indus River in Pakistan. “We will continue fighting against the recent canals and won’t let the state kill us by thirst,” he said. His words came in response to a 945 billion rupee […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 313, "text_sha256": "51bbcf16dc50e7709a6385005d8590df3baedcb6af7c86afbcb0683fe526031f", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.675635+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "945 billion", "start": 292, "end": 303, "evidence": " His words came in response to a 945 billion rupee […]", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.690537+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-28T03:00:39", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan", "start": 3, "end": 11, "matched_text": "Pakistan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "PK", "alpha3": "PAK", "name_zh": "巴基斯坦伊斯兰共和国", "name_en": "Pakistan", "start": 144, "end": 152, "matched_text": "Pakistan", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_961406a62f43e69c0304", "record_id": "article_961406a62f43e69c", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/23052025/ev-hybrid-tax-increase-tucked-into-trumps-big-beautiful-bill", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/23052025/ev-hybrid-tax-increase-tucked-into-trumps-big-beautiful-bill", "title_original": "The Tax Increase Tucked Into Trump’s ‘Big Beautiful Bill’", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-23T18:23:41+00:00", "source_text": "Electric and hybrid vehicle owners should prepare for a big, beautiful tax increase. The text of President Donald Trump’s “big beautiful bill,” which passed the U.S. House of Representatives early Thursday, contains a provision that would impose a new annual registration fee on electric and hybrid vehicles, a move that experts say will disincentivize purchases […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 366, "text_sha256": "0227ef538384c3e04771b264c48450ffabe224ac5102fa82d2516df4428eca47", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:49.525928+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:49.537679+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-23T18:23:41", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 161, "end": 165, "matched_text": "U.S.", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_31db22259c93b3bb1beb", "record_id": "article_31db22259c93b3bb", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/bangladesh-protects-sacred-forests-to-strengthen-biodiversity-conservation", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/bangladesh-protects-sacred-forests-to-strengthen-biodiversity-conservation", "title_original": "Bangladesh protects sacred forests to strengthen biodiversity conservation", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-23T11:32:10+00:00", "source_text": "With an aim to protect biodiversity that’s become fragmented and is scattered across the country, Bangladesh is listing all the old, sacred and socially important trees and forests. The Forest Department has been collecting information from the locals in various parts of the country about locations and details of sites that are centuries-old and sacred […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 358, "text_sha256": "dfd69ea8679d7db9f6660bb78cdb76889b013477c1f4030ff6c81195ee368cc4", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.907749+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:10.928317+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-23T11:32:10", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh", "start": 0, "end": 10, "matched_text": "Bangladesh", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "BD", "alpha3": "BGD", "name_zh": "孟加拉国", "name_en": "Bangladesh", "start": 98, "end": 108, "matched_text": "Bangladesh", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_253ef9ef3fa0b0861a3b", "record_id": "article_253ef9ef3fa0b086", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/23052025/anti-immigration-policies-risk-undocumented-people-during-hurricanes", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/23052025/anti-immigration-policies-risk-undocumented-people-during-hurricanes", "title_original": "Hurricane Season Will Be Even Riskier for Undocumented People This Year", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-23T08:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "With Atlantic hurricane season on the horizon, experts warn that the Trump administration’s anti-immigration policies have exacerbated existing risks for undocumented people weathering disasters in the United States. After California, the states with the largest populations of undocumented immigrants are Florida and Texas, both hurricane hot spots. “In emergency management, people who are undocumented are […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 412, "text_sha256": "3bda8767eaa6216f3f03888c4235eed9ffd1d90f4c74d083e0386d63a46d2b51", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:49.607509+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public inves