{"text_id": "text_bc29a2d097f8e4f69b1d", "record_id": "article_bc29a2d097f8e4f6", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20052025/north-carolina-fires-disaster-relief-subcontractor-founded-by-former-rebuild-nc-boss", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20052025/north-carolina-fires-disaster-relief-subcontractor-founded-by-former-rebuild-nc-boss", "title_original": "NC Fires a Disaster Relief Subcontractor Founded by Former ReBuild NC Boss", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-20T13:38:13+00:00", "source_text": "The North Carolina Division of Emergency Management last week fired a subcontractor that had been founded by top officials at ReBuild NC, the now discredited state agency that botched response efforts after hurricanes Matthew and Florence in 2016 and 2018. The company, PathBuilt, had been hired to work on disaster recovery in western North Carolina. […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 355, "text_sha256": "518b8be2e543b733a37b06648186b349ebbc4c616849a7d726b6c88b82beaa86", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:55.247257+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:55.279882+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-20T13:38:13", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_13ff80cd594fd5aa6e84", "record_id": "article_13ff80cd594fd5aa", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20052025/michigan-polluter-pay-toxic-site-cleanup", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20052025/michigan-polluter-pay-toxic-site-cleanup", "title_original": "Michigan Lawmakers Aim to Revisit ‘Polluter Pay’ to Enforce Cleanup of Toxic Sites", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-20T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Michigan lawmakers are again aiming to boost state environmental cleanup standards and force polluting industries to rehabilitate brownfield sites. “Polluter pay” legislation, facing broad opposition from Republicans, failed last year but Democrats said they are engaging with industry stakeholders to craft laws that will target the worst sites and offenders. Democratic Sen. Jeff Irwin and […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 395, "text_sha256": "97871a0d294a593ec61f623b9d8f3c8061cb674b0e2f65f0b1b823917418ff99", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:55.335528+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:51:55.368416+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-20T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_ced4db9016d6f3a67b3d", "record_id": "article_ced4db9016d6f3a6", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/how-extreme-droughts-could-redefine-the-future-of-amazonian-fish", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/how-extreme-droughts-could-redefine-the-future-of-amazonian-fish", "title_original": "How extreme droughts could redefine the future of Amazonian fish", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-19T10:58:49+00:00", "source_text": "MANAUS, Brazil — In September 2024, the landscape in the Middle Solimões region of the Brazilian Amazon lay in stark contrast to its usual exuberance of lush greenery. “When we were arriving in Tefé and the plane approached to land, I was shocked to see everything very dry, with sandbanks multiplying in the waters,” says […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 326, "text_sha256": "449260cf063f4fe56cc353d485ef83fc88f428939c31a9268529422debff89af", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:15.929241+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:15.949316+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-19T10:58:49", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 8, "end": 14, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_580665c1b08c171c453c", "record_id": "article_580665c1b08c171c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/brazils-offshore-wind-farms-could-sacrifice-small-scale-fishing-in-ceara", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/brazils-offshore-wind-farms-could-sacrifice-small-scale-fishing-in-ceara", "title_original": "Brazil’s offshore wind farms could sacrifice small-scale fishing in Ceará", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-15T15:02:02+00:00", "source_text": "A symbol of Brazil’s Ceará state and present on its official coat of arms since 1897, sail rafts known as jangadas are 80% of the fishing vessels in the state, but they could lose ground to wind turbines installed at sea. The matter is relevant because small-scale fishers who use unmotorized sail rafts such as […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 315, "text_sha256": "9fe6865cc1a6c151dcdd24ffbf6b182ece07949b4cb8463d46c5cb5ba463c083", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:16.135068+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "80%", "start": 119, "end": 122, "evidence": "A symbol of Brazil’s Ceará state and present on its official coat of arms since 1897, sail rafts known as jangadas are 80% of the fishing vessels in the state, but they could lose ground to wind turbines installed at sea.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:16.156836+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-15T15:02:02", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 0, "end": 6, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 12, "end": 18, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7dd750a8b8a8960c0efe", "record_id": "article_7dd750a8b8a8960c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/borneo-project-hopes-to-prove-that-forests-and-oil-palms-can-coexist", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/borneo-project-hopes-to-prove-that-forests-and-oil-palms-can-coexist", "title_original": "Borneo project hopes to prove that forests and oil palms can coexist", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-15T00:50:33+00:00", "source_text": "The Kinabatangan River is the last major area in Malaysian Borneo’s Sabah state with a semblance of forest corridor linking the interior rainforest with mangroves on the east coast, according to Marc Ancrenaz, scientific director of Sabah-based NGO Hutan. It’s a hub for biodiversity, with orangutans, proboscis monkeys and pygmy elephants among the threatened species […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 372, "text_sha256": "b43b2a4918a5595c361e38d157f9564dc97dee945e691243369075b42ab6dca5", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:16.220040+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.