{"text_id": "text_3c58af04dd73bb72b4d0", "record_id": "article_3c58af04dd73bb72", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/solar-panel-manufacturing-is-booming-in-red-states", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2025/05/solar-panel-manufacturing-is-booming-in-red-states", "title_original": "Solar panel manufacturing is booming in red states", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-12T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Transcript: In Georgia, Alabama, Texas, and many other states, factories are churning out solar panels. Gallagher: “We’ve now got five times as much solar panel manufacturing capacity in the U.S. as we did just two years ago.” And Sean Gallaghe r, senior vice president for policy at the Solar Energy Industries Association, says there’s more growth to come. Gallagher: “That success in establishing factories to manufacture solar panels is now starting to pay off in the form of bringing the upstream supply chain back to the U.S. as well.” For example, a large solar panel manufacturer in Georgia is expanding its operations so it can produce solar cells and other components that go into solar panels.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 704, "text_sha256": "32cd34f190e332bb56a65798168a204ba925f0b92073960f74c90fd3aea454fd", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:57.698526+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 90, "end": 95, "evidence": "Transcript: In Georgia, Alabama, Texas, and many other states, factories are churning out solar panels. Gallagher: “We’ve now got five times as much solar panel manufacturing capacity in the U.S. as we did just two years ago.” And Sean"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:57.723878+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-12T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 33, "end": 38, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_4e854cc1cde7636ceb44", "record_id": "article_4e854cc1cde7636c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/a-migrating-flycatcher-returning-to-the-same-sri-lankan-garden-sparks-interest-in-birders", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/a-migrating-flycatcher-returning-to-the-same-sri-lankan-garden-sparks-interest-in-birders", "title_original": "A migrating flycatcher returning to the same Sri Lankan garden sparks interest in birders", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-11T04:35:56+00:00", "source_text": "COLOMBO — As October drew to a close last year, ardent birdwatcher Moditha Kodikarachchi eagerly awaited a special guest in his garden — a migratory Asian paradise flycatcher. Since 2021, the same male flycatcher, identified by three distinct white dots on its black head, has returned to the garden each year, making 2024 its fourth […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 337, "text_sha256": "e8a42e27ca54384687cf78bcb4955d4fe8d1fe50536c2c70e1a8b5e537dd5942", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:22.684488+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:22.716024+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-11T04:35:56", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_60a2b1db067f999bf548", "record_id": "article_60a2b1db067f999b", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/10052025/dry-winter-colorado-river-reservoirs", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/10052025/dry-winter-colorado-river-reservoirs", "title_original": "A Dry Winter on the Colorado River Has Big Reservoirs on Track for Trouble", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-10T08:50:00+00:00", "source_text": "If you took a look at a map of Rocky Mountain snow right now you would see a lot of red. The mountains that feed the Colorado River with snowmelt are strikingly dry, with many ranges holding less than 50 percent of their average snow for this time of year. The low totals could spell […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 287, "text_sha256": "97c1470c1b7ea7263d586b75f038c319147bf0b00cd53e33b3caef4904782788", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:02.566287+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "50 percent", "start": 201, "end": 211, "evidence": " The mountains that feed the Colorado River with snowmelt are strikingly dry, with many ranges holding less than 50 percent of their average snow for this time of year.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:02.579656+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-10T08:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_85bc4cfb82a9c237add2", "record_id": "article_85bc4cfb82a9c237", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/worlds-top-seafood-firms-lobby-against-ocean-conservation-measures-report", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/05/worlds-top-seafood-firms-lobby-against-ocean-conservation-measures-report", "title_original": "World’s top seafood firms lobby against ocean conservation measures: Report", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-05-08T17:27:36+00:00", "source_text": "The world’s biggest seafood companies might seem to have a vested interest in healthy marine ecosystems and plentiful fish stocks. Many claim a commitment to biodiversity in their public messaging. Yet a new report shows they mostly lobby against environmental protections. InfluenceMap, a U.K.-based NGO, released the report on April 10. It assesses the biodiversity-related […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 379, "text_sha256": "48fc7704503e73d98cfa40a2daa0045de5f8e0704db1773ba830f7f2cb6b7be3", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:23.120998+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "GB", "alpha3": "GBR", "name_zh": "英国", "name_en": "United Kingdom"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "GB", "alpha3": "GBR", "name_zh": "英国", "name_en": "United Kingdom"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:23.174785+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-05-08T17:27:36", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "GB", "alpha3": "GBR", "name_zh": "英国", "name_en": "United Kingdom", "start": 290, "end": 294, "matched_text": "U.K.", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.574692+00:00"}
