{"text_id": "text_09824fede611702fe74e", "record_id": "article_09824fede611702f", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/05022025/mid-atlantic-states-prepare-for-disaster-trump-considers-funding-cuts", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/05022025/mid-atlantic-states-prepare-for-disaster-trump-considers-funding-cuts", "title_original": "Mid-Atlantic States Prepare for More Billion-Dollar Disasters as Trump Considers Cutting Emergency Funding", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-05T10:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "PHILADELPHIA—In 2024, Pennsylvania endured a record number of the nation’s billion-dollar weather disasters, from winter storms to drought: 12. Even adjusting for inflation, that’s more than the state faced over the entire decade of the 1980s. Last week, representatives from government, academia, medicine and activism gathered at Drexel University in Philadelphia to tackle an urgent […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 389, "text_sha256": "7037f8c24c4fe36e4d948541eadae83d92b11586a42b699ee35ae3c32b90b517", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:58.171611+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 131, "end": 138, "evidence": "d a record number of the nation’s billion-dollar weather disasters, from winter storms to drought: 12. Even adjusting for inflation, that’s more than the state faced over the entire decade of the 1980s. Last week, representatives from go"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:58.199928+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-05T10:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_871c4bed981362abb7e3", "record_id": "article_871c4bed981362ab", "canonical_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/justice/citizens-and-state-at-odds-over-chiles-rucalhue-dam", "publisher_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/justice/citizens-and-state-at-odds-over-chiles-rucalhue-dam", "title_original": "Citizens and state at odds over Chile’s Rucalhue dam", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Dialogue Earth", "source_id": "INT009", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T18:25:53+00:00", "source_text": "Fernanda Purrán was raised alongside the Biobío River in central Chile. She says the river was “part of our family”, but the arrival of hydropower in the region in the 1990s destroyed that relationship. She says that subsequently, the levels of the waters they swam in would rise at any moment, with no warning as to when a dam’s floodgates would open. “There have been years of uncertainty and a lot of pain, a lot of anguish.” Now, another hydropower plant is on the horizon in Biobío. The Rucalhue project is located less than a kilometre from its namesake village, and 10 kilometres from the communes of Santa Bárbara and Quilaco. The project involves the construction of a power plant and a reservoir.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 706, "text_sha256": "ae611ccd646c3639706d03c8f95091aaf7fbbdaeaf191736d2e1513c658d88cf", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.707075+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 330, "end": 335, "evidence": "s of the waters they swam in would rise at any moment, with no warning as to when a dam’s floodgates would open. “There have been years of uncertainty and a lot of pain, a lot of anguish.” Now, another hydropower plant is on the horizo"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://dialogue.earth/en/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.742049+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T18:25:53", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile", "start": 32, "end": 37, "matched_text": "Chile", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile", "start": 65, "end": 70, "matched_text": "Chile", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_120196fa76fa04743c08", "record_id": "article_120196fa76fa0474", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/study-highlights-effects-of-habitat-fragmentation-on-sri-lankan-specialist-birds", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/study-highlights-effects-of-habitat-fragmentation-on-sri-lankan-specialist-birds", "title_original": "Study highlights effects of habitat fragmentation on Sri Lankan specialist birds", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T16:31:53+00:00", "source_text": "COLOMBO — Forest fragmentation is considered one of the main threats to biodiversity. Many believe this primarily affects small creatures like amphibians and small mammals, while mobile creatures such as birds are less impacted due to their ability to fly. However, new research coming out of Sri Lanka shows how forest fragmentation can restrict even […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 355, "text_sha256": "cd78afa3782d4dbbd1d0afe947e0f5e9f4b6d0c8d724a81bc79911e756b25c39", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.770070+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "LK", "alpha3": "LKA", "name_zh": "斯里兰卡", "name_en": "Sri Lanka"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "LK", "alpha3": "LKA", "name_zh": "斯里兰卡", "name_en": "Sri Lanka"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.782972+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T16:31:53", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "LK", "alpha3": "LKA", "name_zh": "斯里兰卡", "name_en": "Sri Lanka", "start": 293, "end": 302, "matched_text": "Sri Lanka", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_1dff46da6d52d7651080", "record_id": "article_1dff46da6d52d765", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/researchers-make-the-case-for-shift-from-economic-growth-to-human-well-being-within-planetary-limits", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/researchers-make-the-case-for-shift-from-economic-growth-to-human-well-being-within-planetary-limits", "title_original": "Researchers make the case for shift from economic growth to human well-being within planetary limits", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T14:46:04+00:00", "source_text": "For more than a century, nations have measured societal gains in terms of economic growth. But a new review published in the journal Lancet Planetary Health in January 2025 questions that convention. It concludes that humanity would benefit more if it aims for ecological sustainability and stays within the limits of what Earth can provide, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 345, "text_sha256": "a870401d9213f5763228962efee41d63a5f5f06b1e99b125911e301f6ed37ae0", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.807098+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.834728+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T14:46:04", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_cd14c4139f7524a2fdba", "record_id": "article_cd14c4139f7524a2", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/brazilian-soy-farms-and-cattle-pastures-close-in-on-a-land-where-the-grass-is-golden", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/brazilian-soy-farms-and-cattle-pastures-close-in-on-a-land-where-the-grass-is-golden", "title_original": "Brazilian soy farms and cattle pastures close in on a land where the grass is golden", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T12:21:38+00:00", "source_text": "JALAPÃO, Brazil — The buritis, or moriche palms, are fighting for their lives in the streambed now lined with scorched earth. For two years now, drought has advanced a barrier of dead vegetation through this once-humid oasis, called a vereda by the people who live in the Jalapão region of central Brazil. A crested caracara […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 328, "text_sha256": "7631f4751ee6c15d554a41f6c880d4c22f2ffce3e7444361303f7fafb588037a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.863134+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 145, "end": 152, "evidence": "ghting for their lives in the streambed now lined with scorched earth. For two years now, drought has advanced a barrier of dead vegetation through this once-humid oasis, called a vereda by the people who live in the Jalapão region of ce"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:12.875251+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T12:21:38", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 9, "end": 15, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_176d0cf2c6d4850e976c", "record_id": "article_176d0cf2c6d4850e", "canonical_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/nature/in-nagaland-conservation-and-entrepreneurship-go-hand-in-hand", "publisher_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/nature/in-nagaland-conservation-and-entrepreneurship-go-hand-in-hand", "title_original": "In Nagaland, conservation and entrepreneurship go hand in hand", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Dialogue Earth", "source_id": "INT009", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T10:55:50+00:00", "source_text": "In order to preserve Nagaland’s unique cultural, social and economic characteristics, Article 371A of the Indian constitution grants special provisions to the state. The act states that the central government won’t interfere in the religious and social practices of the Nagas, their customary laws and procedures, including civil and criminal justice matters, and ownership or transfer of land and resources, unless the state’s legislative assembly passes a resolution to do so. One significant aspect of this provision is the protection of the traditional landholding system of Nagaland. The state follows a communal land ownership system, where land is owned and managed by tribal communities, clans and villages, or even privately held by individuals.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 754, "text_sha256": "a6c63850042b3b0701d8d3c00b1156b7ba03eea606b6f2c88b7fecffdd609cb3", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.768691+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 126, "end": 131, "evidence": "ue cultural, social and economic characteristics, Article 371A of the Indian constitution grants special provisions to the state. The act states that the central government won’t interfere in the religious and social practices of the N"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://dialogue.earth/en/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.827732+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T10:55:50", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_698aede3fc656088d0f3", "record_id": "article_698aede3fc656088", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/04022025/trump-administration-epa-staff-pronouns-emails-websites", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/04022025/trump-administration-epa-staff-pronouns-emails-websites", "title_original": "Trump Administration Scrubs EPA Staff’s Pronouns from Their Emails and Websites Without Their Knowledge", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T10:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Last Wednesday the Trump administration directed all federal agencies to remove any references to “gender ideology” on websites and email accounts in a two-page memo. Staff had until 5 p.m. Friday to comply with an executive order Donald Trump issued his first day in office on “defending women from gender ideology extremism and restoring biological […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 354, "text_sha256": "c34814de738a7e2b3c75c6e91b57cd8e63b65eb69e415504ce7aec5d00d78be5", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:58.456216+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:52:58.472270+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T10:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_3c8e755b1a8faa11ce7d", "record_id": "article_3c8e755b1a8faa11", "canonical_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/ocean/how-european-companies-feed-the-global-shadow-fleet", "publisher_url": "https://dialogue.earth/en/ocean/how-european-companies-feed-the-global-shadow-fleet", "title_original": "How European companies feed the global shadow fleet", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Dialogue Earth", "source_id": "INT009", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-04T08:07:16+00:00", "source_text": "On 19 July 2024, the oil tanker Hafnia Nile was nearing its top speed when it collided with the supertanker Ceres I, off the east coast of Malaysia. Within minutes, flames engulfed both vessels, sending thick plumes of toxic smoke into the air. Several crew members were airlifted to safety, while others remained on board Ceres I to battle the blaze alongside tugboats. Editor’s note Shadow Fleet Secrets is an ongoing investigative project initiated by Follow the Money in collaboration with Dialogue Earth. Thirteen other newsrooms are involved, including SourceMaterial, Süddeutsche Zeitung, the Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project, and Inside Story, as well as 40 journalists from around the world.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 716, "text_sha256": "f770d33beee56fc6a5eae63603898f5c769d28d939fac0a784c442942c4c710d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.837416+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MY", "alpha3": "MYS", "name_zh": "马来西亚", "name_en": "Malaysia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MY", "alpha3": "MYS", "name_zh": "马来西亚", "name_en": "Malaysia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://dialogue.earth/en/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.870134+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-04T08:07:16", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MY", "alpha3": "MYS", "name_zh": "马来西亚", "name_en": "Malaysia", "start": 139, "end": 147, "matched_text": "Malaysia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_22bebfef58583067aab1", "record_id": "article_22bebfef58583067", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/amazon-states-lead-rebellion-on-environmental-enforcement", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2025/02/amazon-states-lead-rebellion-on-environmental-enforcement", "title_original": "Amazon states lead rebellion on environmental enforcement", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2025-02-03T13:14:33+00:00", "source_text": "In effect for the past 18 years, the soy moratorium seemed established in Brazil. The voluntary agreement in which large soy traders commit to not buying soy from Amazon areas deforested after 2008 had helped to maintain the country’s reputation in international markets. According to the Brazilian Vegetable Oil Industries Association (Abiove), which gathers some of the world’s largest soy companies, this commitment contributed to a 69% reduction in deforestation until 2022. In 2024, however, the agreement suffered an unexpected setback. In July, Rondônia state approved a law punishing its members by withdrawing their fiscal tax incentives. The biggest strike, however, came in October, when a similar law was approved in Mato Grosso.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 741, "text_sha256": "4962a0e4676a084fe579ad6d81a61b9d0e76086c43151e44a8b1b0d9d3f6776c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:17.583028+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "69%", "start": 436, "end": 439, "evidence": " According to the Brazilian Vegetable Oil Industries Association (Abiove), which gathers some of the world’s largest soy companies, this commitment contributed to a 69% reduction in deforestation until 2022.", "interpretation": "target_or_commitment"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "subsidy", "label_zh": "补贴与激励", "label_en": "Subsidies and incentives", "start": 636, "end": 645, "evidence": "July, Rondônia state approved a law punishing its members by withdrawing their fiscal tax incentives. The biggest strike, however, came in October, when a similar law was approved in Mato Grosso."}], "policy_stages": [{"id": "adopted", "label_zh": "通过", "label_en": "Adopted", "start": 567, "end": 575, "evidence": ". In 2024, however, the agreement suffered an unexpected setback. In July, Rondônia state approved a law punishing its members by withdrawing their fiscal tax incentives. The biggest strike, however, came in October, when a similar law wa"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:17.603565+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2025-02-03T13:14:33", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 74, "end": 80, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_e