been put on formal notice by its federal counterpart to force […]"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:19.148842+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-13T10:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_9b9af4eb0663692e994b", "record_id": "article_9b9af4eb0663692e", "canonical_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/revealed-english-farmers-received-record-high-flood-relief-after-last-winters-extreme-rain", "publisher_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/revealed-english-farmers-received-record-high-flood-relief-after-last-winters-extreme-rain", "title_original": "Revealed: English farmers received record-high flood relief after last winter’s extreme rain", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Carbon Brief", "source_id": "INT001", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-12T14:18:30+00:00", "source_text": "English farmers received tens of millions of pounds more in flood-relief funding in 2024 than in any year over the past decade, following intense rainfall last winter. The Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra) recently paid £57.5m from the farming recovery fund to farmers who were hit by extreme rain and floods between October 2023 and March 2024. This is 75 times more than the amount paid out the last time the fund opened to applicants, which was £768k in 2020, according to figures released to Carbon Brief. It is also more than six times higher than all of the payments dispersed between 2015 and 2020, which totalled £9.4m.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 652, "text_sha256": "353c07b8c1d30be116d39d42e7760159161e5e32d8c643e7969d38feb149435d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:32.785879+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 60, "end": 65, "evidence": "English farmers received tens of millions of pounds more in flood-relief funding in 2024 than in any year over the past decade, following intense rainfall last winter. The Department for Environment, Food "}], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 73, "end": 80, "evidence": "English farmers received tens of millions of pounds more in flood-relief funding in 2024 than in any year over the past decade, following intense rainfall last winter. The Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affai"}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:32.819189+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-12T14:18:30", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_6abf571639c7afe08caa", "record_id": "article_6abf571639c7afe0", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/12122024/arizona-attorney-general-sues-industrial-farm-over-water-use", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/12122024/arizona-attorney-general-sues-industrial-farm-over-water-use", "title_original": "In a First, Arizona’s Attorney General Sues an Industrial Farm Over Its Water Use", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-12T09:55:00+00:00", "source_text": "PHOENIX—Arizona Attorney General Kris Mayes filed a nuisance lawsuit against an industrial agricultural operation Wednesday in a novel case that alleges the operation’s groundwater pumping is threatening public health and safety and the infrastructure of the surrounding community. Mayes hopes the suit sends a message that pushes state legislators to pass new laws managing groundwater […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 390, "text_sha256": "9519295f3c3d2df17fc36739efc440141d18b8c066b07c46a11903f7e770c74a", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:19.328808+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:19.347995+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-12T09:55:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_48a203cd705139475a05", "record_id": "article_48a203cd70513947", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/12/in-2024-nepals-elusive-snow-leopards-pounce-into-spotlight", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/12/in-2024-nepals-elusive-snow-leopards-pounce-into-spotlight", "title_original": "In 2024, Nepal’s elusive snow leopards pounce into spotlight", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-12T06:43:43+00:00", "source_text": "KATHMANDU — The elusive snow leopard (Panthera uncia), often described as the “ghost of the mountains,” has captivated the imagination of researchers, the general public and mountain communities for centuries. Fables related to this enigmatic big cat have been handed down from generation to generation, weaving a sense of mystery and reverence for the cat […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 360, "text_sha256": "ccef6f62f6abadc886949d59bb9aed96fb7ac2701b3a198f9900e8cf0e304046", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:41.553827+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:41.566491+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-12T06:43:43", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal", "start": 9, "end": 14, "matched_text": "Nepal", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_2a4ccaa07a9d2581668f", "record_id": "article_2a4ccaa07a9d2581", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/12/how-much-should-you-worry-about-a-collapse-of-the-atlantic-conveyor-belt", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/12/how-much-should-you-worry-about-a-collapse-of-the-atlantic-conveyor-belt", "title_original": "How much should you worry about a collapse of the Atlantic conveyor belt?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-11T12:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Several high-profile research papers have brought renewed attention to the potential collapse of a crucial system of ocean currents known as the Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation, or AMOC, as we discussed in part one of this two-part post. Huge uncertainties in both the timing and details of potential impacts of such a collapse remain. Even so, scientists warned in a recent open letter that “such an ocean circulation change would have devastating and irreversible impacts.” The AMOC is a vast oceanic loop that carries warm water northward through the uppermost Atlantic toward Iceland and Greenland, where it cools and descends before returning southward. The Gulf Stream, which carries warm water from the tropics toward Europe, is an important section of this loop.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 782, "text_sha256": "f443d6809d3f8851d511b46f22299630a629ca3568a2ea15178e96090b8972b7", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:47.103507+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "IS", "alpha3": "ISL", "name_zh": "冰岛", "name_en": "Iceland"}, {"alpha2": "GL", "alpha3": "GRL", "name_zh": "格陵兰", "name_en": "Greenland"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "IS", "alpha3": "ISL", "name_zh": "冰岛", "name_en": "Iceland"}, {"alpha2": "GL", "alpha3": "GRL", "name_zh": "格陵兰", "name_en": "Greenland"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:47.143062+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-11T12:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "IS", "alpha3": "ISL", "name_zh": "冰岛", "name_en": "Iceland", "start": 592, "end": 599, "matched_text": "Iceland", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "GL", "alpha3": "GRL", "name_zh": "格陵兰", "name_en": "Greenland", "start": 604, "end": 613, "matched_text": "Greenland", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_e5107cf54f8f96c6674f", "record_id": "article_e5107cf54f8f96c6", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/12/environmental-journalist-in-cambodia-shot-and-killed-by-suspected-logger", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/12/environmental-journalist-in-cambodia-shot-and-killed-by-suspected-logger", "title_original": "Environmental journalist in Cambodia shot and killed by suspected logger", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-11T09:52:00+00:00", "source_text": "SIEM REAP, Cambodia — Chhoeung Chheng, a journalist covering environmental issues for local online news outlet Kampuchea Aphiwat News, has died of his injuries after being shot in Siem Reap province on Dec. 4 by a suspected illegal logger. Chheng was rushed to a commune health clinic with a gunshot wound to the abdomen before being […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 337, "text_sha256": "1c1533e3bea189da4469fb30728ee7c8d737d70a3d8af91e6a10bfe04639c80c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:41.644263+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "KH", "alpha3": "KHM", "name_zh": "柬埔寨", "name_en": "Cambodia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "KH", "alpha3": "KHM", "name_zh": "柬埔寨", "name_en": "Cambodia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:41.658304+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-12-11T09:52:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "KH", "alpha3": "KHM", "name_zh": "柬埔寨", "name_en": "Cambodia", "start": 28, "end": 36, "matched_text": "Cambodia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "KH", "alpha3": "KHM", "name_zh": "柬埔寨", "name_en": "Cambodia", "start": 11, "end": 19, "matched_text": "Cambodia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.575747+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_2fa7f975a9f5ce313463", "record_id": "article_2fa7f975a9f5ce31", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06122024/philadelphia-mach2-hydrogen-hub-challenges", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/06122024/philadelphia-mach2-hydrogen-hub-challenges", "title_original": "It’s Do or Die Time for Philly Hydrogen Hub, and Some Green Groups Are Rooting for Death", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-12-06T10:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "PHILADELPHIA—As energy wonks descended on a downtown hotel for a hydrogen conference, witches were waiting for them in the parking lot. Donning a black, horned hat and green face paint, Delaware Riverkeeper Maya van Rossum and a coven of fellow protesters played off the release of the movie “Wicked” to lambast what they see as […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 332, "text_sha256": "d73ed518f9bdfbbef45e36050e97b698e5b70d64f59d122e076887459742723b", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:20.252377+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 16, "end": 22, "evidence": "PHILADELPHIA—As energy wonks descended on a downtown hotel for a hydrogen conference, witches were waiting for them in the parking lot. Donning a black, horned ha"}], "poli