{"text_id": "text_11260f3206447098c6c2", "record_id": "article_11260f3206447098", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/11/rafael-one-of-just-three-cat2-november-hurricanes-in-the-gulf-of-mexico", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/11/rafael-one-of-just-three-cat2-november-hurricanes-in-the-gulf-of-mexico", "title_original": "Rafael one of just three Cat2+ November hurricanes in the Gulf of Mexico", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-07T15:19:06+00:00", "source_text": "[Haz clic aquí para leer en español] Hurricane Rafael made landfall in southwestern Cuba about 40 miles southwest of Havana at 4:15 pm. EST Wednesday, Nov. 6, as a category 3 storm with 115 mph (185 km/h) winds and a central pressure of 956 mb. Rafael was the first November major hurricane to make landfall in Cuba since Hurricane Michelle of 2001. Traveling northwest, Rafael passed about 30 miles (50 km) west of Havana, where top sustained winds of 44 mph (71 km/h), gusting to 71 mph (114 km/h), were measured at 3:50 p.m. EST. Rafael’s powerful winds caused major disruptions to Cuba’s electrical power grid, triggering an island-wide power failure just days after Cuba’s grid suffered a complete failure Oct. 18-22.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 722, "text_sha256": "97338a6babf066f389aab7b1a34e1f14c8c81fc8a1c40cad206131e4eed07cd4", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:55.984460+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "CU", "alpha3": "CUB", "name_zh": "古巴", "name_en": "Cuba"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CU", "alpha3": "CUB", "name_zh": "古巴", "name_en": "Cuba"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:48:56.030236+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-11-07T15:19:06", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 66, "end": 72, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "CU", "alpha3": "CUB", "name_zh": "古巴", "name_en": "Cuba", "start": 84, "end": 88, "matched_text": "Cuba", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.576363+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_dc7d624a37da489b8c4e", "record_id": "article_dc7d624a37da489b", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/11/indonesia-fisheries-minister-eyes-aquaculture-expansion-under-prabowo", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/11/indonesia-fisheries-minister-eyes-aquaculture-expansion-under-prabowo", "title_original": "Indonesia fisheries minister eyes aquaculture expansion under Prabowo", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-06T14:02:43+00:00", "source_text": "JAKARTA, Indonesia — Sakti Wahyu Trenggono, who will remain as Indonesia’s fisheries minister in the administration of new President Prabowo Subianto, has unveiled an ambitious target to revitalize 78,000 hectares (about 200,000 acres) of unproductive shrimp ponds along Java’s northern coast. Officials hope that many of these sites, some of which have been dormant for […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 374, "text_sha256": "b08a60da9f87d080a1432ae671385b717bc67547f5db785e19af9fbb055f0f5e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:57.443586+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:57.460531+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-11-06T14:02:43", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia", "start": 0, "end": 9, "matched_text": "Indonesia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia", "start": 9, "end": 18, "matched_text": "Indonesia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.576363+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_7e40444d7249a0272085", "record_id": "article_7e40444d7249a027", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/11/new-standard-for-ethical-palm-oil-faces-backlash-before-its-even-issued", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/11/new-standard-for-ethical-palm-oil-faces-backlash-before-its-even-issued", "title_original": "New standard for ethical palm oil faces backlash before it’s even issued", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-06T11:47:28+00:00", "source_text": "JAKARTA — The world’s top certification body for ethical palm oil is set to vote on a major new standard aimed at balancing conservation goals with the practicalities of the palm oil industry. This revised standard, expected to pass at the annual general assembly of the Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil (RSPO) on Nov. 13 […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 327, "text_sha256": "8c173e1828a44c9b9022f3bbaff2469ae58f2cc164ab8aaffe51a2695904be3c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:02.403014+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:02.415608+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-11-06T11:47:28", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.576363+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_95da17102509b7e8d9ba", "record_id": "article_95da17102509b7e8", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03112024/lake-ice-coverage-research", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03112024/lake-ice-coverage-research", "title_original": "As Ice Coverage of Lakes Decreases, Scientists Work to Understand What Happens Under Water in Winter", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-03T09:50:00+00:00", "source_text": "During the summer months, much of life in lakes is limited to areas near the shore where light touches the bottom. But on the first day of ice-over in winter, a fish could look up and see a vast and temporary micro-ecosystem containing mats of algae and dozens of microorganisms buzzing around. For Stephanie Hampton, […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 321, "text_sha256": "6e2832632b30ab5e1cb8e340649a231755e8dd0dc50c7d6edcabdc7270f91ca4", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:39.303535+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:39.316917+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-11-03T09:50:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.576363+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_986038baac9c235000ae", "record_id": "article_986038baac9c2350", "canonical_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/cop16-key-outcomes-agreed-at-the-un-biodiversity-conference-in-cali-colombia", "publisher_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/cop16-key-outcomes-agreed-at-the-un-biodiversity-conference-in-cali-colombia", "title_original": "COP16: Key outcomes agreed at the UN biodiversity conference in Cali, Colombia", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Carbon Brief", "source_id": "INT001", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-02T18:31:18+00:00", "source_text": "Print article Share The COP16 biodiversity summit came to an abrupt halt after countries failed to reach consensus on the creation of a new fund during a mammoth 10-hour final plenary session. Countries debated through the night on Friday in Cali, Colombia, in an attempt to get through the many items on COP16’s agenda. But, as the talks dragged on into Saturday morning, a large number of developing-country delegates were forced to catch flights home, leaving parties without the “quorum” needed to reach consensus on key issues. Countries did manage to find consensus on a new benefit-sharing mechanism for genetic resources – known as the “Cali fund” – after lengthy discussions and last-minute text changes put forward by India to protect sovereign rights.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 762, "text_sha256": "9255a3df24ced83cbb2d7e6aec46650fbf872f4a5ba54c738be77df96f06e1c3", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.749527+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": ["COP16"], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "negotiations", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:46:40.786063+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-11-02T18:31:18", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia", "start": 70, "end": 78, "matched_text": "Colombia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia", "start": 248, "end": 256, "matched_text": "Colombia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "IN", "alpha3": "IND", "name_zh": "印度", "name_en": "India", "start": 728, "end": 733, "matched_text": "India", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.576363+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f77c99a3dbdf7e4c7f80", "record_id": "article_f77c99a3dbdf7e4c", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/01112024/how-can-we-close-natures-funding-gap", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/01112024/how-can-we-close-natures-funding-gap", "title_original": "How Can We Close Nature’s Funding Gap?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-11-01T19:34:59+00:00", "source_text": "Over the past two weeks, leaders from more than 175 countries have gathered in Cali, Colombia, for the 16th gathering of parties to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity. The topic at hand? Preventing the utter collapse of nature, which is well underway, according to a wide body of research. A suite of strategies […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 334, "text_sha256": "c589a62193e0ab305c749a988f757e2ea04de8fb81e1577d3fa5f01c1c543986", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:53:39.480426+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CO", "alpha3": "COL", "name_zh": "哥伦比亚", "name_en": "Colombia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "