{"text_id": "text_84a12c5765219f9c0d71", "record_id": "article_84a12c5765219f9c", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/to-protect-the-planets-rangelands-give-pastoralists-a-boost-un-report-says", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/to-protect-the-planets-rangelands-give-pastoralists-a-boost-un-report-says", "title_original": "To protect the planet’s rangelands, give pastoralists a boost, UN report says", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-07-05T09:41:42+00:00", "source_text": "When it comes to conservation, forests and oceans are the big attention grabbers. But rangelands, which cover 54% of the planet’s terrestrial surface, are no less important for nature and wildlife. With ecosystems as varied as deserts, grasslands, semiarid shrublands and savannas, a third of global biodiversity hotspots fall within rangelands. More than 40% of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 366, "text_sha256": "b8e363607269b50985d74091b6f671979e9f352673c0fda5e53f1655dbd8d81f", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:01.331328+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "54%", "start": 110, "end": 113, "evidence": " But rangelands, which cover 54% of the planet’s terrestrial surface, are no less important for nature and wildlife.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}, {"value_text": "40%", "start": 356, "end": 359, "evidence": " More than 40% of […]", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:01.348263+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-07-05T09:41:42", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_ebce9d987012fcb49a49", "record_id": "article_ebce9d987012fcb4", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/how-philanthropy-in-asia-is-evolving", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/how-philanthropy-in-asia-is-evolving", "title_original": "How philanthropy in Asia is evolving", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-07-04T09:54:23+00:00", "source_text": "In a world grappling with increasingly complex environmental and social challenges, the role of philanthropy is undergoing a profound transformation, particularly in Asia. The recent Philanthropy Asia Summit underscored this evolution, highlighting how new funding mechanisms and collaborative approaches are reshaping the philanthropic landscape. The summit, organized by the Philanthropy Asia Alliance (PAA) and held […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 422, "text_sha256": "2511a3d04bd47a60f0146cfe699adbeeed9db507ff6f0b154f3d7c8fce2ea4e4", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:01.396185+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 257, "end": 264, "evidence": "sia. The recent Philanthropy Asia Summit underscored this evolution, highlighting how new funding mechanisms and collaborative approaches are reshaping the philanthropic landscape. The summit, organized by the Philanthropy Asia Alliance "}], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:01.412219+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-07-04T09:54:23", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_ba0a011cb1fbf9e42bec", "record_id": "article_ba0a011cb1fbf9e4", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03072024/south-america-hydrogen-plan-threatens-bird-sanctuary", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03072024/south-america-hydrogen-plan-threatens-bird-sanctuary", "title_original": "In Chile’s Southern Tip, a Bet on Hydrogen Worries Conservationists", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-07-03T09:05:00+00:00", "source_text": "The birds are like clouds in Bahía Lomas. Far off in the southern tip of South America, in the province of Tierra del Fuego, migration takes its highest form in this bay in the eastern mouth in the Straits of Magellan. Here, thousands of birds, like the Red Knot, congregate each winter after flying over […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 308, "text_sha256": "80d7097b3dcf8c599da82572c3d23fd15f2cf1c6711e3a617fb6d872544b8dc4", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:30.729173+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:30.739687+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-07-03T09:05:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CL", "alpha3": "CHL", "name_zh": "智利", "name_en": "Chile", "start": 3, "end": 8, "matched_text": "Chile", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_335693a31ffe5ae7cb8d", "record_id": "article_335693a31ffe5ae7", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02072024/worker-heat-protection-standards", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/02072024/worker-heat-protection-standards", "title_original": "First Heat Protection Standards for Workers Proposed by Biden Administration", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-07-02T21:01:56+00:00", "source_text": "President Joe Biden’s administration unveiled its long-awaited proposal to protect workers from extreme heat at what might appear to be an appropriate time—amid a record-hot summer with millions of Americans sweltering under heat advisories. But the Occupational Health and Safety Administration proposed the nation’s first heat injury and illness protection standards on the heels of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 388, "text_sha256": "f7fb2604944de2ca79213dc7057878ea4ab0fca4f12e113968e3f7b8437c781e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:30.787362+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [{"id": "proposed", "label_zh": "提出", "label_en": "Proposed", "start": 63, "end": 71, "evidence": "President Joe Biden’s administration unveiled its long-awaited proposal to protect workers from extreme heat at what might appear to be an appropriate time—amid a record-hot summer with millions of Americans swe"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:30.802023+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-07-02T21:01:56", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_77bf091bad30236dc8e0", "record_id": "article_77bf091bad30236d", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/as-the-world-burns-can-we-learn-to-live-with-wildfire-health-risks", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/07/as-the-world-burns-can-we-learn-to-live-with-wildfire-health-risks", "title_original": "As the world burns, can we learn to live with wildfire health risks?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-07-02T15:20:08+00:00", "source_text": "As dry brush crackled and smoke curled upward, there was a palpable feeling of satisfaction among firefighters gathered near Cranbrook in the Canadian province of British Columbia. It was a sunny day in April, and if the weather held, the multiagency team hoped to quickly finish a prescribed burn on 42 hectares (104 acres) of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 331, "text_sha256": "751639376c6367b46f77286cd9e1d8b167dadc557e770196b1a17d9c444f2faf", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:01.530859+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CA", "alpha3": "CAN", "name_zh": "加拿大", "name_en": "Canada"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CA", "alpha3": "CAN", "name_zh": "加拿大", "name_en": "Canada"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_