{"text_id": "text_0fd7242c7087f31098b1", "record_id": "article_0fd7242c7087f310", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/environmental-protests-under-attack-interview-with-un-special-rapporteur-michel-forst", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/environmental-protests-under-attack-interview-with-un-special-rapporteur-michel-forst", "title_original": "Environmental protests under attack: Interview with UN special rapporteur Michel Forst", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-24T16:25:07+00:00", "source_text": "Events in February felt like a legal double whammy for the environment and its defenders. First, the United Nations Environment Assembly declined a Bolivian proposal to grant rights to nature and Mother Earth. Then, Michel Forst, the U.N. special rapporteur on environmental defenders under the Aarhus Convention, raised the alarm with his new paper: “State […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 361, "text_sha256": "4624ab216fc9c3acc77026b9cec005874eacf072add3e017c017a8ea24186d2c", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.207438+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [{"id": "investment", "label_zh": "公共投入与融资", "label_en": "Public investment and finance", "start": 169, "end": 174, "evidence": "defenders. First, the United Nations Environment Assembly declined a Bolivian proposal to grant rights to nature and Mother Earth. Then, Michel Forst, the U.N. special rapporteur on environmental defenders under the Aarhus Convention, "}], "policy_stages": [{"id": "proposed", "label_zh": "提出", "label_en": "Proposed", "start": 157, "end": 165, "evidence": "ent and its defenders. First, the United Nations Environment Assembly declined a Bolivian proposal to grant rights to nature and Mother Earth. Then, Michel Forst, the U.N. special rapporteur on environmental defenders under the Aarhus Con"}], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.220347+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-24T16:25:07", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_2a9b6afc6552fdae6534", "record_id": "article_2a9b6afc6552fdae", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/forced-evictions-suppress-maasai-spirituality-sacred-spaces-in-tanzania", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/forced-evictions-suppress-maasai-spirituality-sacred-spaces-in-tanzania", "title_original": "Forced evictions suppress Maasai spirituality & sacred spaces in Tanzania", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-22T01:39:56+00:00", "source_text": "When the dawn breaks over Kisokon village in Kenya’s Narok county, Maasai herders leave their bomas, tend to their cattle and follow them around as they graze in nearby pastures. But this is rarely the morning routine of Mokompo Ole Simel, one of Africa’s oldest oloiboni, a traditional spiritual leader. Simel, in his 90s, wakes […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 333, "text_sha256": "5ee89766e0ab2a6131f19caae0be5c8e907870e834f85b25cfe92dce22fec38e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.303292+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "TZ", "alpha3": "TZA", "name_zh": "坦桑尼亚", "name_en": "Tanzania"}, {"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.316025+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-22T01:39:56", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "TZ", "alpha3": "TZA", "name_zh": "坦桑尼亚", "name_en": "Tanzania", "start": 65, "end": 73, "matched_text": "Tanzania", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "KE", "alpha3": "KEN", "name_zh": "肯尼亚", "name_en": "Kenya", "start": 45, "end": 50, "matched_text": "Kenya", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_d4027bc32674d81a0e09", "record_id": "article_d4027bc32674d81a", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/the-most-prominent-mining-companies-in-the-pan-amazon-a-review", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/the-most-prominent-mining-companies-in-the-pan-amazon-a-review", "title_original": "The most prominent mining companies in the Pan Amazon – a review", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-21T16:24:29+00:00", "source_text": "Vale SA Brazil’s second most valuable company is also the fifth largest global mining corporation. In 2022, it was as ranked by the Refinitiv ESG framework as best in its class of ‘diversified miners’ (1 out of 615). This score is remarkable considering Vale is being sued by the SEC for deliberately misleading investors of […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 328, "text_sha256": "0845b519f13561f3b53c5de2d93f8e99ca633fc47b5e10c2311793e0ba7e10a7", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.325989+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.338325+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-21T16:24:29", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "BR", "alpha3": "BRA", "name_zh": "巴西", "name_en": "Brazil", "start": 8, "end": 14, "matched_text": "Brazil", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_601f48d37ed2c3d73f73", "record_id": "article_601f48d37ed2c3d7", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/flash-floods-hit-mexico-coastal-flooding-reaches-texas-as-alberto-makes-landfall", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/flash-floods-hit-mexico-coastal-flooding-reaches-texas-as-alberto-makes-landfall", "title_original": "Flash floods hit Mexico, coastal flooding reaches Texas as Alberto makes landfall", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-20T20:07:42+00:00", "source_text": "[Lee en español] The center of lopsided Tropical Storm Alberto pushed ashore just before dawn Thursday, June 20, near Tampico, Mexico. Alberto’s top sustained winds were estimated at 50 mph just prior to landfall. The system quickly decayed to a tropical depression by 11 a.m. EDT as it moved inland, and Alberto was predicted to be a remnant low by Thursday night. In Tampico itself, the impacts from Alberto were minimal. Sustained winds at the international airport peaked at a mere 21 mph, with peak gusts to 29 mph, and little rain fell in the drought-stricken city. However, Alberto’s tentacles stretched far more broadly than usual for a tropical storm.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 660, "text_sha256": "49154448cb243cd7a3992b3d511eabc6d91e808c9e8c907375867bc3f073201b", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.654130+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 549, "end": 556, "evidence": "l airport peaked at a mere 21 mph, with peak gusts to 29 mph, and little rain fell in the drought-stricken city. However, Alberto’s tentacles stretched far more broadly than usual for a tropical storm."}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.691973+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-20T20:07:42", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 17, "end": 23, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 50, "end": 55, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 127, "end": 133, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_ce0bd130d7e844102e17", "record_id": "article_ce0bd130d7e84410", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/from-the-amazon-to-the-himalayas-an-invasive-catfish-makes-its-nepal-debut", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/06/from-the-amazon-to-the-himalayas-an-invasive-catfish-makes-its-nepal-debut", "title_original": "From the Amazon to the Himalayas, an invasive catfish makes its Nepal debut", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-20T11:16:56+00:00", "source_text": "KATHMANDU — The discovery in a Nepali river of an armored catfish native to the Amazon has alarmed researchers and conservationists, who say it’s still not clear how the species found its way from the South American rainforest to the Himalayan nation. Forty-three specimens of Pterygoplichthys disjunctivus, known as the vermiculated sailfin catfish, were discovered […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 370, "text_sha256": "cb5b1da353e9f36b641511072380dbde5f14b07349980a8ff521c7ecda561bbc", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.420257+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:07.432662+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-20T11:16:56", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal", "start": 64, "end": 69, "matched_text": "Nepal", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_abd87aa4811a363a1cc6", "record_id": "article_abd87aa4811a363a", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/mountaintop-coal-mine-in-kentucky-to-become-a-solar-farm", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/mountaintop-coal-mine-in-kentucky-to-become-a-solar-farm", "title_original": "Mountaintop coal mine in Kentucky to become a solar farm", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-20T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "Across Appalachia, coal mines are closing. And people are trying to figure out what to do with former mine lands, including mountaintops that were blasted off to get to the coal underneath. Albrecht: “So you end up with this almost like plateau-like landscape … with hundreds of acres at a time that are almost pancake flat.” Joseph Albrecht is with BrightNight , a solar developer. He says some reclaimed mine land is well-suited for solar development — both because of that flat wide-open terrain and because it’s already been developed with roads and power lines.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 566, "text_sha256": "265b9be3192df32a5daf7a7212f6ae43adff3e15f79a6abfa3c8cfdd514f846d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.705206+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 19, "end": 23, "evidence": "Across Appalachia, coal mines are closing. And people are trying to figure out what to do with former mine lands, including mountaintops that were blasted off to g"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.740044+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-20T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_76101be07a9d3dbcd0e2", "record_id": "article_76101be07a9d3dbc", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20062024/europes-new-esg-rules-spark-questions-about-what-sustainable-investing-looks-like", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/20062024/europes-new-esg-rules-spark-questions-about-what-sustainable-investing-looks-like", "title_original": "Europe’s New ESG Rules Spark Questions About What Sustainable Investing Looks Like", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-20T09:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "The European Union’s move to tighten rules for sustainable investing will put two-thirds of Europe’s so-called ESG funds on notice, forcing thousands of them to either sell off $40 billion in assets or change their names in a way that more accurately and transparently reflects their holdings. Last month, the European Securities and Markets Authority […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 355, "text_sha256": "9834e5b53c58f2ebd57e00e347d3851536df7b3e05a6e531bd7301a33bb89812", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:36.937678+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "$40 billion", "start": 177, "end": 188, "evidence": "The European Union’s move to tighten rules for sustainable investing will put two-thirds of Europe’s so-called ESG funds on notice, forcing thousands of them to either sell off $40 billion in assets or change their names in a way that more accurately and transparently reflects their holdings.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:54:36.951508+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-20T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577387+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c32112bf9e3a61fa34e6", "record_id": "article_c32112bf9e3a61fa", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/tropical-storm-alberto-batters-northeastern-mexico-and-texas", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/06/tropical-storm-alberto-batters-northeastern-mexico-and-texas", "title_original": "Tropical Storm Alberto batters northeastern Mexico and Texas", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-06-19T16:31:21+00:00", "source_text": "The first tropical storm of what’s expected to be a rip-roaring 2024 Atlantic season – Alberto – was hurtling toward an expected landfall in northeast Mexico after being officially named at 11 a.m. EDT Wednesday, June 19. Tropical storm warnings were in effect for most of the west coast of the Gulf of Mexico, extending from Tecolutla, Mexico, well north to San Luis Pass, Texas. Even before the storm was named, Alberto’s huge, lopsided wind field drove a large storm surge of 3-4 feet to the central and upper Texas coast during the high tide cycle on Wednesday morning. Major coastal flooding occurred from Freeport to Galveston, including Surfside Beach (see video below).", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 677, "text_sha256": "46d0dbbe49cdd4fbef0de97d08aabb99d9adc8ed479b1c58659c6965bb45005e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.819353+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 588, "end": 593, "evidence": "tral and upper Texas coast during the high tide cycle on Wednesday morning. Major coastal flooding occurred from Freeport to Galveston, including Surfside Beach (see video below)."}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:49:50.868385+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-06-19T16:31:21", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 44, "end": 50, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 55, "end": 60, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "MX", "alpha3": "MEX", "name_zh": "墨西哥", "name_en": "Mexico", "start": 151, "end": 157, "matched_text": "Mexico", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 374, "end": 379, "matched_text": "Texas", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_