 could usually be found clad in at least three layers of clothing to protect"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:18.156773+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-03-19T09:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_9e1586c776f05b4e66f0", "record_id": "article_9e1586c776f05b4e", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/03/un-probes-controversial-forest-carbon-agreement-in-malaysian-borneo", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/03/un-probes-controversial-forest-carbon-agreement-in-malaysian-borneo", "title_original": "UN probes controversial forest carbon agreement in Malaysian Borneo", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-03-18T20:01:08+00:00", "source_text": "The state government of Sabah in Malaysian Borneo has reaffirmed its plans to proceed with an opaque nature conservation agreement despite concerns raised by the United Nations. Representatives of Sabah’s government and a representative of a Singaporean company called Hoch Standard Pte. Ltd. signed the agreement, which included the rights to carbon and other marketable […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 375, "text_sha256": "bcd414d22a3e7e57d455b892b4250bcbecd68d459a01c439475263ec2cff5606", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:57.833070+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:57.849325+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-03-18T20:01:08", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_f69874a4ede90aeee53f", "record_id": "article_f69874a4ede90aee", "canonical_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/drill-baby-drill-the-surprising-history-of-donald-trumps-fossil-fuel-slogan", "publisher_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/drill-baby-drill-the-surprising-history-of-donald-trumps-fossil-fuel-slogan", "title_original": "‘Drill, baby, drill’: The surprising history of Donald Trump’s fossil-fuel slogan", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Carbon Brief", "source_id": "INT001", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-03-18T16:46:33+00:00", "source_text": "As Donald Trump prepares for this year’s US presidential election, he continues to summarise his energy policies with one simple slogan: “Drill, baby, drill.” The Republican candidate has laid claim to the phrase, arguing that more drilling will allow him to cut inflation and flood the country with the “ liquid gold ” that is oil. However, it was Michael Steele , the US politician who served as the first African-American lieutenant governor of Maryland and chair of the Republican National Committee, who came up with the slogan back in 2008. Speaking to Carbon Brief, Steele stresses that Trump had “nothing to do” with “drill, baby, drill” – a phrase he coined to promote US independence from Middle Eastern oil.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 718, "text_sha256": "c08fc29cce7179701f41a119e622c9265d25aa1e61fd6dd245eea733d4dc1026", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:18.296526+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "energy", "label_zh": "能源与产业", "label_en": "Energy and industry", "start": 97, "end": 103, "evidence": "ld Trump prepares for this year’s US presidential election, he continues to summarise his energy policies with one simple slogan: “Drill, baby, drill.” The Republican candidate has laid claim to the phrase, arguing that more drilling wi"}, {"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 277, "end": 282, "evidence": " laid claim to the phrase, arguing that more drilling will allow him to cut inflation and flood the country with the “ liquid gold ” that is oil. However, it was Michael Steele , the US politician who served as the first African-Americ"}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:18.328499+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-03-18T16:46:33", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 41, "end": 43, "matched_text": "US", "method": "country-acronym-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_c56855748fd6731be97f", "record_id": "article_c56855748fd6731b", "canonical_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/03/californias-new-megafires-are-taking-a-toll-on-wildlife-habitat-researchers-find", "publisher_url": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/2024/03/californias-new-megafires-are-taking-a-toll-on-wildlife-habitat-researchers-find", "title_original": "California’s new megafires are taking a toll on wildlife habitat, researchers find", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Yale Climate Connections", "source_id": "INT008", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-03-18T11:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "California’s long-toed salamanders are one of the species threatened by rising rates of extreme fire in the state. Named for the unusual length of one of its hind toes, this salamander is typically dark gray or black with yellow or green markings on its back and measures up to three inches long from snout to vent. During massive California wildfires in 2020 and 2021, about 14% of the long-toed salamander’s range in the affected areas were burned by high-severity fire — the most of any species studied as part of a broader investigation into the toll of these fires on the region’s wildlife habitat.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 603, "text_sha256": "5aecf00c81b0b59896cc735b1dfb1d7e851ca5a40f684b9dd62e5a662314b09e", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:13.582300+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [{"value_text": "14%", "start": 376, "end": 379, "evidence": " During massive California wildfires in 2020 and 2021, about 14% of the long-toed salamander’s range in the affected areas were burned by high-severity fire — the most of any species studied as part of a broader investigation into the toll of these fires on the region’s wildlife habitat.", "interpretation": "not_classified"}], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "governance_themes": [{"id": "science", "label_zh": "气候科学与风险", "label_en": "Climate science and risk", "start": 342, "end": 350, "evidence": "s back and measures up to three inches long from snout to vent. During massive California wildfires in 2020 and 2021, about 14% of the long-toed salamander’s range in the affected areas were burned by high-severity fire — the most of any "}], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://yaleclimateconnections.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:50:13.601499+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-03-18T11:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 0, "end": 10, "matched_text": "California", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "title_original"}, {"alpha2": "US", "alpha3": "USA", "name_zh": "美国", "name_en": "United States", "start": 0, "end": 10, "matched_text": "California", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do