{"text_id": "text_ac4caf8381eed42e889e", "record_id": "article_ac4caf8381eed42e", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/02/communities-on-troubled-java-river-mold-future-from-plastic-waste", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/02/communities-on-troubled-java-river-mold-future-from-plastic-waste", "title_original": "Communities on troubled Java river mold future from plastic waste", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-02-01T03:55:45+00:00", "source_text": "BOGOR, Indonesia — At the age of 60, Siti Salamah started making changes at her family home in the city of Bogor, just south of Jakarta, Indonesia’s capital. “We always put the kitchen waste there,” Siti told Mongabay Indonesia at her home. “I collect the plastic waste separately.” Siti installed a unit for composting perishable […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 334, "text_sha256": "60289a86eaa179972cf0d911b93c5b3338c7c5f3c56de876de267765b6f60c28", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:56:19.004500+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:56:19.018995+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-02-01T03:55:45", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "ID", "alpha3": "IDN", "name_zh": "印度尼西亚", "name_en": "Indonesia", "start": 7, "end": 16, "matched_text": "Indonesia", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_60934d82311faf99dfad", "record_id": "article_60934d82311faf99", "canonical_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/qa-what-progress-has-been-made-on-protecting-nature-a-year-on-from-cop15", "publisher_url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/qa-what-progress-has-been-made-on-protecting-nature-a-year-on-from-cop15", "title_original": "Q&A: What progress has been made on protecting nature a year on from COP15?", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Carbon Brief", "source_id": "INT001", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-01-31T11:32:54+00:00", "source_text": "It has been more than one year since the gavel came down at the last UN biodiversity summit, where almost every country in the world agreed on a plan to protect nature. The Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework was signed off at the COP15 summit in Montreal, Canada in December 2022. (See Carbon Brief’s in-depth summary of the key outcomes.) The landmark deal contained a number of goals and targets for countries to achieve over the coming years – such as setting aside land for wildlife, reducing pesticide risks and restoring ecosystems. In the months since, more nature pledges have been announced, a new biodiversity fund was established and more science showing the impacts of humans on nature has been published.", "text_kind": "article_excerpt", "text_characters": 729, "text_sha256": "e5a577462a9fd5940a4626face7c2076f9fdfd0224946a3f1c275724fbb2bb78", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_content_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:30.441355+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": ["COP15"], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "CA", "alpha3": "CAN", "name_zh": "加拿大", "name_en": "Canada"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "negotiations", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "CA", "alpha3": "CAN", "name_zh": "加拿大", "name_en": "Canada"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:47:30.515538+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-01-31T11:32:54", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [{"alpha2": "CA", "alpha3": "CAN", "name_zh": "加拿大", "name_en": "Canada", "start": 268, "end": 274, "matched_text": "Canada", "method": "country-span-v2", "source_field": "source_text"}], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_361fa304fd01ceb46fa6", "record_id": "article_361fa304fd01ceb4", "canonical_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/31012024/nevada-supreme-court-groundwater-restrictions", "publisher_url": "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/31012024/nevada-supreme-court-groundwater-restrictions", "title_original": "Environmentalists See Nevada Supreme Court Ruling Bringing State’s Water Management ‘Into the 21st Century’", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Inside Climate News", "source_id": "INT004", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-01-31T10:00:00+00:00", "source_text": "The Nevada Supreme Court unanimously ruled last week that the state can restrict new groundwater pumping if it will impact other users and wildlife, a decision that strikes a blow to the plan of a developer that at one time hoped to build a new city of 250,000 people in the Mojave Desert and could […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 302, "text_sha256": "c2bc3766d8923874dab2cd705b1723731449dfc1aae5acfa00a2e09c84ca170d", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:39.064632+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://insideclimatenews.org/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:55:39.092617+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-01-31T10:00:00", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_5c845c25041f4446ccf8", "record_id": "article_5c845c25041f4446", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/01/to-ease-deforestation-natural-rubber-industry-must-paddle-hard-commentary", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/01/to-ease-deforestation-natural-rubber-industry-must-paddle-hard-commentary", "title_original": "To ease deforestation, natural rubber industry must ‘paddle hard’ (commentary)", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-01-30T00:07:13+00:00", "source_text": "Last October, I took some time off work at the Global Platform for Sustainable Natural Rubber (GPSNR) to learn how to surf. Surfing has always been a dream of mine and one of the more advanced surfing techniques is learning how to ride green waves (also known as unbroken waves). The image of surfers carving […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 312, "text_sha256": "162bc3bc79a865f6e48ffeecf3d581c3b913f42811188e822264ab7d5b206096", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:56:23.669403+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evidence-v1", "review_status": "machine_extracted_not_human_verified", "archive_source_endpoint": "https://news.mongabay.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts", "archive_collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:56:23.688453+00:00", "published_at_raw": "2024-01-30T00:07:13", "sample_frame": "public_archives_20261102", "sampling_method": "deterministic_uniform_url_hash", "sampling_probability": 0.30234709214938144, "country_evidence": [], "country_tag_version": "country-span-v2", "quarantine_reason": "stored_excerpt_and_headline_do_not_establish_climate_scope", "quarantined_at": "2026-11-02T02:09:04.577910+00:00"}
{"text_id": "text_2ab79346154524262c05", "record_id": "article_2ab7934615452426", "canonical_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/01/nepals-low-altitude-snow-leopard-would-face-big-hurdles-in-return-to-wild", "publisher_url": "https://news.mongabay.com/2024/01/nepals-low-altitude-snow-leopard-would-face-big-hurdles-in-return-to-wild", "title_original": "Nepal’s ‘low-altitude’ snow leopard would face big hurdles in return to wild", "title_zh": null, "title_en": null, "summary_zh": null, "summary_en": null, "source_name": "Mongabay", "source_id": "INT007", "source_type": "professional_climate_media", "language": "en", "published_at": "2024-01-28T08:32:43+00:00", "source_text": "LALITPUR, Nepal — As the gates to the vet clinic at the Central Zoo in Lalitpur opened, more than two dozen photojournalists thronged the facility and surrounded a metal cage aiming their DSLR cameras at a snow leopard (Panthera uncia) inside. “Please don’t come close to the animal,” the zoo’s vet, Radha Krishna Gharti, told […]", "text_kind": "source_excerpt", "text_characters": 330, "text_sha256": "af809d7a76298f1bd9a07ec1116aea02d0622efd293f0b642e9ad2856ea33ec7", "text_basis": "public_wordpress_excerpt", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T01:56:23.813310+00:00", "extractor_version": "1.0.0", "document_type": "source_report", "document_type_basis": "document_genre_not_independently_established", "event_date": null, "event_date_precision": null, "source_updated_at": null, "policy_direction": null, "legal_effect": null, "summary_model": null, "quantitative_claims": [], "conference_ids": [], "agenda_item_id": null, "thematic_day_id": null, "rights_status": "source_attributed_excerpt_not_full_text", "country_codes": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal"}], "governance_themes": [], "policy_tools": [], "policy_stages": [], "track": "action", "country_mentions": [{"alpha2": "NP", "alpha3": "NPL", "name_zh": "尼泊尔", "name_en": "Nepal"}], "annotation_method": "dictionary-evi